{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202610260606346c3047d3300448af","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Very useful. Line 286 confirms: Г. Јеремић, „Мозаици Медијане – нека разматрања\", Ниш и Византија IV, Ниш 2006, pp. 153, 157 — where she discusses the \"Mediana octagon\" (baptistery vs luxury residential building debate). So Jeremić 2006 at p. 153, 157 discusses the octagon building being possibly another luxury residential object (villa), not a baptistery. This is relevant to the \"objects\" question — the \"građevina sa oktogonom\" (building with octagon).\n\nAlso the earlier reference (line 208): Јеремић Г, \"Мозаици грађевине са октогоном из Античког Наиса\", Ниш и Византија 5, Ниш, 2007 — \"Mosaics of the building with the octagon from ancient Naissus\" — Niš i Vizantija 5. So there is a Jeremić 2007 paper too, in Niš i Vizantija V. Probably also on ubnt.ni.ac.rs: http://www.ubnt.ni.ac.rs/images/pdf/nisivizantija/Nis%20i%20Vizantija%20-%2005.../...Jeremic...\n\nWait, actually — is the \"građevina sa oktogonom iz Antičkog Naisa\" the Mediana octagon? The villa with octagon at Mediana (\"Amadžijska njiva\") — yes, \"građevina sa oktogonom\" is part of the Mediana complex (building with octagonal and circular room, north of the horreum, per line 190: \"северно грађевина са кружном и октогоналном просторијом\"). So Jeremić 2007 in Niš i Vizantija 5 is about mosaics of that building. \n\nNow — the site nisandbyzantium.org.rs is mentioned (line 284): http://www.nisandbyzantium.org.rs/ — the \"Niš i Vizantija\" symposium website. The zbornici PDFs are hosted there. Also the old ubnt.ni.ac.rs URL.\n\nNow let me try the webReader again (rate limit may have reset) for:\n1. http://www.ubnt.ni.ac.rs/images/pdf/nisivizantija/Nis%20i%20Vizantija%20-%2004_2005/10_Jeremic_Gordana.pdf — direct PDF of Jeremić 2006.\n2. http://www.nisandbyzantium.org.rs/ — main site, look for zbornik IV and V.\n\nNote: the webReader error \"-400: Please Enter the Correct URL Format!\" for the Bing URL with quotes/encoded chars. For the PDF URL with %20 encodings it might also fail... Let me try. Actually the first call failed with -400 because of the encoded quotes maybe. The second (unencoded with spaces? no — \"https://www.bing.com/search?q=Mozaici+Medijane+Jeremic\" — valid) failed with -429 rate limit. So the format rule may reject some URLs. Let me try the direct PDF URL (encoded) and if -400, try alternate.\n\nActually, maybe try the nisandbyzantium.org.rs site first since it's the official host. The old URL path on ubnt.ni.ac.rs is likely dead (the site moved). The nisandbyzantium.org.rs site has \"Zbornik radova\" PDFs. Let me try fetching http://www.nisandbyzantium.org.rs/ and see.\n\nWait — but the WebFetch tool is denied, only mcp webReader is available and rate-limited. Let me be careful with each call. Also there might be a per-minute limit; I'll space calls with local file reads in between.\n\nLet me also check what remains in the local files: academia_urbanism.html (Academia page for Milošević Urbanism — not core to my current task, that's task #1 of ZADATAK but coordinator's current priorities are Jeremić-focused), gb1/gb2 (Google Books), ia1 (Internet Archive), hathi1 — those were for Petrović 1994 monograph probably. fasti_search.html, fasti_n.html — FASTI records for Mediana excavations (2007+ reports by Narodni muzej Niš — could mention objects A-D!). Let me grep fasti files for Jeremić/objekat.\n\nPriority: my final report needs:\n1. Jeremić 2006 full text — try to get it (ubnt.ni.ac.rs PDF URL).\n2. 2009 abstract — find venue. The abstract format with \"Institute of Archaeology, Belgrade (Serbia)\" and 1-page — this looks like abstracts from a conference. Possibly \"XVII Limes Congress\"? Or \"The 14th International Colloquium on Roman Mosaics\"? Hmm — could be from \"Mosaics of Greece and the Roman world\"? Or from the annual \"Skoplje symposium\"? Actually — it might be from the conference \"Rome and the Provinces\"? Let me search SCIndeks for Jeremić's 2009 paper. There is a known publication: Jeremić G., \"New Archaeological Data on the Mosaics in Mediana near Niš\", possibly in \"Felix Romuliana\" or... Actually I recall the conference \"Naissus et Byzantium\"? Hmm.\n\nWait — where did the previous session download jeremic_mozaici_2009.pdf from? The log would say. Let me grep the log for \"jeremic_mozaici_2009\" or \"2009\".","signature":"c25df15533234667850e000e"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"call_228a9101adba430ca741f6e2","session_id":"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d","uuid":"8d24f39f-fee2-4758-8f16-133321ebd678","timestamp":"2026-10-25T22:06:51.303Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Lov na Jeremić 2006 mozaici"}
