dc:type>publishedVersion</dc:type>\n<dc:identifier>https://rai.ai.ac.rs/handle/123456789/938</dc:identifier>\n<dc:identifier>http://rai.ai.ac.rs/bitstream/id/2150/35_AIHV_2018_abstract.pdf</dc:identifier>\n<dc:identifier>https://hdl.handle.net/21.15107/rcub_rai_938</dc:identifier>\n<dc:language>en</dc:language>\n<dc:relation>info:eu-repo/grantAgreement/MESTD/Basic Research (BR or ON)/177007/RS//</dc:relation>\n<dc:rights>openAccess</dc:rights>\n<dc:rights>https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/</dc:rights>\n<dc:rights>ARR</dc:rights>\n<dc:publisher>Association Internationale pour l'Histoire du Verre</dc:publisher>\n<dc:source>21st Congress of the Association Internationale pour l'Histoire du Verre, Istanbul-Turkey, 3rd-7th September 2018, Abstracts / Résumés, 2018, 59.</dc:source>\n</oai_dc:dc></metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:rai.ai.ac.rs:123456789/939</identifier><datestamp>2023-11-27T11:10:01Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_123456789_1</setSpec><setSpec>col_123456789_3</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/\" xmlns:doc=\"http://www.lyncode.com/xoai\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\" xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\" xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd\">\n<dc:title>Recent finds of the Roman and late antique glass from Naissus (Niš, SRB)</dc:title>\n<dc:creator>Jeremić, Gordana</dc:creator>\n<dc:creator>Čerškov, Toni</dc:creator>\n<dc:subject>Naissus / Niš / glass findings / vessels / windowpanes / necropolises / domus / Roman period / Late Antiquty</dc:subject>\n<dc:description>The Roman and late antique city Naissus which is preserved below layers of modern and middle age cities of Niš has been researched for more than 150 years with various intensities and it is, however, known to a very modest extent. During extensive excavations due to the need for underground passage construction performed in 1990-1991 at the left bank of Nišava river, registered were the late antique necropolis within occupational layers from the end of the 1st to the mid-3rd centuries. At this area was registered a certain number of glass vessels from different archaeological units that are the subject of various analyses of style and context within this contribution. Here will be also taken into consideration the recent glass findings (2009-2015) from another larger necropolis of Naissus at the right bank of Nišava river formed along the road to Rataria (Arčar, BG). During the protective archaeological excavations at the area of the luxurious domus (the assumed late antique imperial palace) intra muros of the Naissus fortification during 1987-1988 explored late antique and early Byzantine layers dated from the second half of the 4th to 6th centuries. In these layers were found glass materials (lamps, vessels, windowpanes) that provide data on the period and the way of the usage of this unique space that through these periods experienced its transformations from luxurious representative building to modest residential units and added workshops. Glass artefacts from these excavations belong to the standard late antique repertoire with parallels in numerous localities within Naissus and its vicinity.</dc:description>\n<dc:date>2023-11-23T11:37:19Z</dc:date>\n<dc:date>2023-11-23T11:37:19Z</dc:date>","numLines":55,"startLine":27900,"totalLines":71039}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_da50a50577e241d1aa7c7366","type":"tool_result","content":"29400\t<dc:rights>openAccess</dc:rights>\n29401\t<dc:rights>ARR</dc:rights>\n29402\t<dc:publisher>Београд : Археолошки институт</dc:publisher>\n29403\t<dc:source>Mnemosynon firmitatis : Седамдесет година Археолошког института (1947-2017), Београд 2017, 138-139</dc:source>\n29404\t</oai_dc:dc></metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:rai.ai.ac.rs:123456789/977</identifier><datestamp>2023-12-31T19:15:39Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_123456789_1</setSpec><setSpec>col_123456789_3</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/\" xmlns:doc=\"http://www.lyncode.com/xoai\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\" xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\" xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd\">\n29405\t<dc:title>Некропола у Јагодин Мали, Ниш (Naissus) : касноантичко наслеђе између чувања и уништавања</dc:title>\n29406\t<dc:creator>Jeremić, Gordana</dc:creator>\n29407\t<dc:contributor>Марицки-Гађански, Ксенија</dc:contributor>\n29408\t<dc:subject>Ниш / Наисус / касноантичка некропола / истраживања / методологија / заштита налазишта</dc:subject>\n29409\t<dc:description>Представља се историјат истраживања касноантичке и ранохришћанске некрополе Наисуса у градској четврти Јагодин Мали, са развојем институција, које су се старале о истраживању, заштити и презентацији, до приказа стања и угрожености овог културног наслеђа у оквиру насељене урбане зоне, која се интензивно изграђује, без адекватних археолошких интервенција.</dc:description>\n29410\t<dc:date>2023-11-23T12:23:10Z</dc:date>\n29411\t<dc:date>2023-11-23T12:23:10Z</dc:date>\n29412\t<dc:date>2017</dc:date>\n29413\t<dc:type>conferenceObject</dc:type>\n29414\t<dc:type>publishedVersion</dc:type>\n29415\t<dc:identifier>978-86-89367-08-9</dc:identifier>\n29416\t<dc:identifier>https://rai.ai.ac.rs/handle/123456789/977</dc:identifier>\n29417\t<dc:identifier>http://rai.ai.ac.rs/bitstream/id/2208/32_DRUSTVO_ZA_ANT_STUDIJE_2017_abstract.pdf</dc:identifier>\n29418\t<dc:identifier>https://hdl.handle.net/21.15107/rcub_rai_977</dc:identifier>\n29419\t<dc:language>sr</dc:language>\n29420\t<dc:relation>info:eu-repo/grantAgreement/MESTD/Basic Research (BR or ON)/177007/RS//</dc:relation>\n29421\t<dc:rights>openAccess</dc:rights>\n29422\t<dc:rights>ARR</dc:rights>\n29423\t<dc:publisher>Београд : Дрштво за античке студије Србије</dc:publisher>\n29424\t<dc:source>Антика некад и сад: значај, улога и наслеђе кроз векове. 11. Међународни научни скуп, 16-17. децембар 2017, Књига резимеа</dc:source>\n29425\t</oai_dc:dc></metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:rai.ai.ac.rs:123456789/978</identifier><datestamp>2025-06-12T11:26:00Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_123456789_1</setSpec><setSpec>col_123456789_3</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/\" xmlns:doc=\"http://www.lyncode.com/xoai\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\" xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\" xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd\">\n29426\t<dc:title>Representation of Medusa on a mosaic floor in Mediana</dc:title>\n29427\t<dc:creator>Jeremić, Gordana</dc:creator>\n29428\t<dc:contributor>Vujović, Miroslav B.</dc:contributor>\n29429\t<dc:subject>Mediana / villa with peristyle / aula / floor mosaic / Medusa / late antiquity / 4th century</dc:subject>\n29430\t<dc:description>A number of representative rooms decorated by mosaic floors from the period around the 4th century were examined during the archaeological research of the villa with peristyle in the middle of the late antiquity settlement in Mediana near Naissus. In 1969, a part of the damaged mosaic floor with geometrical motifs and a central round emblem including a representation of Medusa-Gorgon with wings was discovered in the central room of the villa, that is, in a large triclinium-aula. Medusa is represented in the manner of late antiquity, as a woman with a pensive expression who has lost many of the attributes characteristic of such representations in Greek and Hellenistic art. The aim of this paper is not only to provide analyses of the visual artistic aspect of the presentation but also to attempt a reconstruction of the mosaic carpet in the room on the basis of various site data, which are now available to researchers.</dc:description>\n29431\t<dc:date>2023-11-23T12:24:59Z</dc:date>\n29432\t<dc:date>2023-11-23T12:24:59Z</dc:date>\n29433\t<dc:date>2017</dc:date>\n29434\t<dc:type>bookPart</dc:type>\n29435\t<dc:type>publishedVersion</dc:type>\n29436\t<dc:identifier>978-86-6427-068-7</dc:identifier>\n29437\t<dc:identifier>https://rai.ai.ac.rs/handle/123456789/978</dc:identifier>\n29438\t<dc:identifier>http://rai.ai.ac.rs/bitstream/id/2209/05_ANTE_PORTAM_AUREAM_2017_Representation_of_Medusa_on_a_mosaic_floor.pdf</dc:identifier>\n29439\t<dc:identifier>https://hdl.handle.net/21.15107/rcub_rai_978</dc:identifier>\n29440\t<dc:language>en</dc:language>\n29441\t<dc:relation>info:eu-repo/grantAgreement/MESTD/Basic Research (BR or ON)/177007/RS//</dc:relation>\n29442\t<dc:rights>openAccess</dc:rights>\n29443\t<dc:rights>ARR</dc:rights>\n29444\t<dc:publisher>Belgrade : University of Belgrade, Faculty of Philosophy</dc:publisher>\n29445\t<dc:source>Ante portam auream. Studia in honorem professoris Aleksandar Jovanović</dc:source>\n29446\t</oai_dc:dc></metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:rai.ai.ac.rs:123456789/979</identifier><datestamp>2024-05-07T10:19:01Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_123456789_1</setSpec><setSpec>col_123456789_3</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/\" xmlns:doc=\"http://www.lyncode.com/xoai\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\" xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\" xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd\">\n29447\t<dc:title>Грађевина са октогоном у Градском пољу, Ниш : извештај о археолошким истраживањима у 2016. години</dc:title>\n29448\t<dc:creator>Jeremić, Gordana</dc:creator>\n29449\t<dc:creator>Petrovic, Vladimir</dc:creator>\n29450\t<dc:subject>Ниш</dc:subject>\n29451\t<dc:subject>Naissus</dc:subject>\n29452\t<dc:subject>Нишка тврђава</dc:subject>\n29453\t<dc:subject>грађевина са октогоном</dc:subject>\n29454\t<dc:subject>domus</dc:subject>\n29455\t<dc:subject>касна антика</dc:subject>\n29456\t<dc:description>У раду су представљени прелиминарни резултати сондажних билатералних истраживања перистила луксузног домуса у оквиру утврђеног града Наисуса, на локалитету Пешачка стаза.</dc:description>\n29457\t<dc:date>2023-11-23T12:25:39Z</dc:date>\n29458\t<dc:date>2023-11-23T12:25:39Z</dc:date>\n29459\t<dc:date>2016</dc:date>"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d","uuid":"ce5ff9f1-3096-4025-9fe5-8e963852ff91","timestamp":"2026-10-25T22:06:58.808Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Svemir\\data\\sessions\\c1792946760393lb6a\\medijana_baza\\roj_glm\\objekti_CD\\oai_full.xml","content":"<dc:rights>openAccess</dc:rights>\n<dc:rights>ARR</dc:rights>\n<dc:publisher>Београд : Археолошки институт</dc:publisher>\n<dc:source>Mnemosynon firmitatis : Седамдесет година Археолошког института (1947-2017), Београд 2017, 138-139</dc:source>\n</oai_dc:dc></metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:rai.ai.ac.rs:123456789/977</identifier><datestamp>2023-12-31T19:15:39Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_123456789_1</setSpec><setSpec>col_123456789_3</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/\" xmlns:doc=\"http://www.lyncode.com/xoai\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\" xmlns:dc=\