{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_a42ec7afed9b41acbc35394f","type":"tool_result","content":"43870\t<dc:identifier>https://rai.ai.ac.rs/handle/123456789/1538</dc:identifier>\n43871\t<dc:identifier>http://rai.ai.ac.rs/bitstream/id/4422/bitstream_4422.pdf</dc:identifier>\n43872\t<dc:identifier>https://hdl.handle.net/21.15107/rcub_rai_1538</dc:identifier>\n43873\t<dc:language>sr</dc:language>\n43874\t<dc:relation>info:eu-repo/grantAgreement/MESTD/Basic Research (BR or ON)/177007/RS//</dc:relation>\n43875\t<dc:rights>openAccess</dc:rights>\n43876\t<dc:rights>ARR</dc:rights>\n43877\t<dc:publisher>Beograd : Arheološki institut</dc:publisher>\n43878\t</oai_dc:dc></metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:rai.ai.ac.rs:123456789/1539</identifier><datestamp>2026-07-24T08:24:30Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_123456789_1</setSpec><setSpec>col_123456789_3</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/\" xmlns:doc=\"http://www.lyncode.com/xoai\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\" xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\" xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd\">\n43879\t<dc:title>Constantine's Villa at Mediana</dc:title>\n43880\t<dc:creator>Vasić, Miloje</dc:creator>\n43881\t<dc:creator>Milošević, Gordana</dc:creator>\n43882\t<dc:creator>Gavrilović Vitas, Nadežda</dc:creator>\n43883\t<dc:creator>Crnoglavac, Vesna</dc:creator>\n43884\t<dc:subject>Villa with peristyle</dc:subject>\n43885\t<dc:subject>Constantine the Great</dc:subject>\n43886\t<dc:subject>Naissus</dc:subject>\n43887\t<dc:subject>IV century</dc:subject>\n43888\t<dc:subject>palatial complex</dc:subject>\n43889\t<dc:description>Constantine's Villa at Mediana is a monography about the administrative-residential complex of Roman emperor Constantine the Great at Mediana in Niš (antique Naissus). The monograph is based on the newest archaeological results of excavations and research conducted in the area of a large villa with peristyle, thermae and antique gate.</dc:description>\n43890\t<dc:date>2024-01-31T09:56:37Z</dc:date>\n43891\t<dc:date>2024-01-31T09:56:37Z</dc:date>\n43892\t<dc:date>2016</dc:date>\n43893\t<dc:type>book</dc:type>\n43894\t<dc:type>publishedVersion</dc:type>\n43895\t<dc:identifier>978-86-83019-46-5</dc:identifier>\n43896\t<dc:identifier>https://rai.ai.ac.rs/handle/123456789/1539</dc:identifier>\n43897\t<dc:identifier>http://rai.ai.ac.rs/bitstream/id/4423/bitstream_4423.pdf</dc:identifier>\n43898\t<dc:identifier>https://hdl.handle.net/21.15107/rcub_rai_1539</dc:identifier>\n43899\t<dc:language>en</dc:language>\n43900\t<dc:relation>Constantine’s villa at Mediana, financed by the Ministry of Culture and Information of Republic Serbia, no. 451-04-2024/2015-02</dc:relation>\n43901\t<dc:relation>info:eu-repo/grantAgreement/MESTD/Basic Research (BR or ON)/177007/RS//</dc:relation>\n43902\t<dc:rights>openAccess</dc:rights>\n43903\t<dc:rights>ARR</dc:rights>\n43904\t<dc:publisher>Niš: The National Museum Niš</dc:publisher>\n43905\t</oai_dc:dc></metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:rai.ai.ac.rs:123456789/1540</identifier><datestamp>2026-05-07T10:24:07Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_123456789_1</setSpec><setSpec>col_123456789_3</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/\" xmlns:doc=\"http://www.lyncode.com/xoai\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\" xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\" xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd\">\n43906\t<dc:title>Ex Asia et Syria : Oriental Religions in the Roman Central Balkans</dc:title>\n43907\t<dc:creator>Gavrilović Vitas, Nadežda</dc:creator>\n43908\t<dc:subject>Asia Minor</dc:subject>\n43909\t<dc:subject>Syria</dc:subject>\n43910\t<dc:subject>Oriental cults</dc:subject>\n43911\t<dc:subject>Roman Central Balkans</dc:subject>\n43912\t<dc:description>The monograph \"Ex Asia Minor et Syria. Religions in the Roman Central Balkans\" investigates the cults of Asia Minor and Syrian origin in the Roman provinces of the Central Balkans. The author presents, analyzes and interprets all hitherto known epigraphical and archaeological material which attests to the presence of Asia Minor and Syrian cults in that region, a subject which is yet to be the object of a serious scholarly study. Thus the book both reviews previously known monuments and artefacts, many of which are now missing or are destroyed, and adds new finds, exploring their social and geographical context from all possible angles, and focusing on the thoughts and beliefs of the dedicators and devotees of the particular cult in question. New conclusions are presented in a scientific framework, taking account of the latest theoretical developments.</dc:description>\n43913\t<dc:description>Archaeopress Roman Archaeology, vol. 78.</dc:description>\n43914\t<dc:date>2024-01-31T10:06:33Z</dc:date>"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d","uuid":"842c129c-db21-4d88-8045-a9b8348411f3","timestamp":"2026-10-25T22:07:16.617Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Svemir\\data\\sessions\\c1792946760393lb6a\\medijana_baza\\roj_glm\\objekti_CD\\oai_full.xml","content":"<dc:identifier>https://rai.ai.ac.rs/handle/123456789/1538</dc:identifier>\n<dc:identifier>http://rai.ai.ac.rs/bitstream/id/4422/bitstream_4422.pdf</dc:identifier>\n<dc:identifier>https://hdl.handle.net/21.15107/rcub_rai_1538</dc:identifier>\n<dc:language>sr</dc:language>\n<dc:relation>info:eu-repo/grantAgreement/MESTD/Basic Research (BR or ON)/177007/RS//</dc:relation>\n<dc:rights>openAccess</dc:rights>\n<dc:rights>ARR</dc:rights>\n<dc:publisher>Beograd : Arheološki institut</dc:publisher>\n</oai_dc:dc></metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:rai.ai.ac.rs:123456789/1539</identifier><datestamp>2026-07-24T08:24:30Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_123456789_1</setSpec><setSpec>col_123456789_3</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/\" xmlns:doc=\"http://www.lyncode.com/xoai\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\" xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\" xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd\">\n<dc:title>Constantine's Villa at Mediana</dc:title>\n<dc:creator>Vasić, Miloje</dc:creator>\n<dc:creator>Milošević, Gordana</dc:creator>\n<dc:creator>Gavrilović Vitas, Nadežda</dc:creator>\n<dc:creator>Crnoglavac, Vesna</dc:creator>\n<dc:subject>Villa with peristyle</dc:subject>\n<dc:subject>Constantine the Great</dc:subject>\n<dc:subject>Naissus</dc:subject>\n<dc:subject>IV century</dc:subject>\n<dc:subject>palatial complex</dc:subject>\n<dc:description>Constantine's Villa at Mediana is a monography about the administrative-residential complex of Roman emperor Constantine the Great at Mediana in Niš (antique Naissus). The monograph is based on the newest archaeological results of excavations and research conducted in the area of a large villa with peristyle, thermae and antique gate.</dc:description>\n<dc:date>2024-01-31T09:56:37Z</dc:date>\n<dc:date>2024-01-31T09:56:37Z</dc:date>\n<dc:date>2016</dc:date>\n<dc:type>book</dc:type>\n<dc:type>publishedVersion</dc:type>\n<dc:identifier>978-86-83019-46-5</dc:identifier>\n<dc:identifier>https://rai.ai.ac.rs/handle/123456789/1539</dc:identifier>\n<dc:identifier>http://rai.ai.ac.rs/bitstream/id/4423/bitstream_4423.pdf</dc:identifier>\n<dc:identifier>https://hdl.handle.net/21.15107/rcub_rai_1539</dc:identifier>\n<dc:language>en</dc:language>\n<dc:relation>Constantine’s villa at Mediana, financed by the Ministry of Culture and Information of Republic Serbia, no. 451-04-2024/2015-02</dc:relation>\n<dc:relation>info:eu-repo/grantAgreement/MESTD/Basic Research (BR or ON)/177007/RS//</dc:relation>\n<dc:rights>openAccess</dc:rights>\n<dc:rights>ARR</dc:rights>\n<dc:publisher>Niš: The National Museum Niš</dc:publisher>\n</oai_dc:dc></metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:rai.ai.ac.rs:123456789/1540</identifier><datestamp>2026-05-07T10:24:07Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_123456789_1</setSpec><setSpec>col_123456789_3</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/\" xmlns:doc=\"http://www.lyncode.com/xoai\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\" xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\" xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd\">\n<dc:title>Ex Asia et Syria : Oriental Religions in the Roman Central Balkans</dc:title>\n<dc:creator>Gavrilović Vitas, Nadežda</dc:creator>\n<dc:subject>Asia Minor</dc:subject>\n<dc:subject>Syria</dc:subject>\n<dc:subject>Oriental cults</dc:subject>\n<dc:subject>Roman Central Balkans</dc:subject>\n<dc:description>The monograph \"Ex Asia Minor et Syria. Religions in the Roman Central Balkans\" investigates the cults of Asia Minor and Syrian origin in the Roman provinces of the Central Balkans. The author presents, analyzes and interprets all hitherto known epigraphical and archaeological material which attests to the presence of Asia Minor and Syrian cults in that region, a subject which is yet to be the object of a serious scholarly study. Thus the book both reviews previously known monuments and artefacts, many of which are now missing or are destroyed, and adds new finds, exploring their social and geographical context from all possible angles, and focusing on the thoughts and beliefs of the dedicators and devotees of the particular cult in question. New conclusions are presented in a scientific framework, taking account of the latest theoretical developments.</dc:description>\n<dc:description>Archaeopress Roman Archaeology, vol. 78.</dc:description>\n<dc:date>2024-01-31T10:06:33Z</dc:date>","numLines":45,"startLine":43870,"totalLines":71039}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_91cb90401cde404ea042fc41","type":"tool_result","content":"44305\t<dc:identifier>https://rai.ai.ac.rs/handle/123456789/1562</dc:identifier>\n44306\t<dc:identifier>http://rai.ai.ac.rs/bitstream/id/4640/bitstream_4640.pdf</dc:identifier>\n44307\t<dc:identifier>https://hdl.handle.net/21.15107/rcub_rai_1562</dc:identifier>\n44308\t<dc:language>en</dc:language>\n44309\t<dc:rights>openAccess</dc:rights>\n44310\t<dc:rights>ARR</dc:rights>\n44311\t<dc:publisher>Molina de Aragón: Junta de Comunidades de Castilla-La Mancha</dc:publisher>\n44312\t<dc:source>Celtic Religion across Space and Time: fontes epigraphici religionum celticarum antiquarum (IX Workshop F.E.R.C.AN. 17–20 de septiembre 2008)</dc:source>\n44313\t</oai_dc:dc></metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:rai.ai.ac.rs:123456789/1555</identifier><datestamp>2026-07-24T08:24:30Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_123456789_1</setSpec><setSpec>col_123456789_3</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/\" xmlns:doc=\"http://www.lyncode.com/xoai\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\" xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\" xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd\">\n44314\t<dc:title>Carska ideologija u arhitekturi, umetnosti i skulpturi rimske vile na Medijani</dc:title>\n44315\t<dc:creator>Milošević, Gordana</dc:creator>\n44316\t<dc:creator>Gavrilović, Nadežda</dc:creator>\n44317\t<dc:subject>Konstantin Veliki</dc:subject>\n44318\t<dc:subject>Naissus</dc:subject>\n44319\t<dc:subject>carska ideologija</dc:subject>\n44320\t<dc:subject>Medijana</dc:subject>\n44321\t<dc:description>U radu se raspravlja o novim tumacenjima rimske vile na suburbiumu Medijana. Na prostoru Medijane konstatovano i sistematski istraženo više gradevina razlicitih funkcija, kao što su na vila sa peristilom i termama, vila sa oktogonom, skladišta sa radionicama i vojnim barakama, dve ranohrišcanske bazilike, nekropole i više manjih vseoskih vila. Nova arheološka istraživanja vile sa peristilom sprovedenim u periodu od 2010 do 2012. godine omogucila su potpuno sagledavanje i izdvajanje graditeljskih faza, kao i analizu celokupne umetnosti kasnoantickog perioda zastupljenu u fresko-slikarstvu, mozaicima, arhitektonskoj plastici i skulpturi. Jasno je utvrdeno da se promene na vili sa peristilom u reprezentativni rezidencijalni objekat mogu vezati za period i graditeljske poduhvate Konstantina Velikog u Nišu.</dc:description>\n44322\t<dc:date>2024-02-01T11:44:44Z</dc:date>\n44323\t<dc:date>2024-02-01T11:44:44Z</dc:date>\n44324\t<dc:date>2013</dc:date>\n44325\t<dc:type>bookPart</dc:type>\n44326\t<dc:type>publishedVersion</dc:type>\n44327\t<dc:identifier>978-86-7148-176-2</dc:identifier>\n44328\t<dc:identifier>https://rai.ai.ac.rs/handle/123456789/1555</dc:identifier>\n44329\t<dc:identifier>http://rai.ai.ac.rs/bitstream/id/4442/bitstream_4442.pdf</dc:identifier>\n44330\t<dc:identifier>https://hdl.handle.net/21.15107/rcub_rai_1555</dc:identifier>\n44331\t<dc:language>sr</dc:language>\n44332\t<dc:relation>info:eu-repo/grantAgreement/MESTD/Basic Research (BR or ON)/177007/RS//</dc:relation>\n44333\t<dc:rights>openAccess</dc:rights>\n44334\t<dc:rights>ARR</dc:rights>\n44335\t<dc:publisher>Niš : Pravni fakultet Univerziteta u Nišu</dc:publisher>\n44336\t<dc:source>Zbornik radova 1700 godina Milanskog edikta</dc:source>\n44337\t</oai_dc:dc></metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:rai.ai.ac.rs:123456789/1563</identifier><datestamp>2026-05-07T10:24:07Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_123456789_1</setSpec><setSpec>col_123456789_3</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/\" xmlns:doc=\"http://www.lyncode.com/xoai\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\" xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\" xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd\">\n44338\t<dc:title>Thracian Influence in Asia Minor Mystery Cults in the Eastern Parts of the Roman Provinces in the Central Balkans</dc:title>\n44339\t<dc:creator>Gavrilović Vitas, Nadežda</dc:creator>\n44340\t<dc:subject>Asia Minor cults</dc:subject>\n44341\t<dc:subject>Central Balkans</dc:subject>\n44342\t<dc:subject>mistery religions</dc:subject>\n44343\t<dc:subject>funerary rites</dc:subject>\n44344\t<dc:subject>snake</dc:subject>\n44345\t<dc:description>During the period of Roman rule in the Central Balkan Roman provinces,&#xd;\n44346\tamong other oriental cults, like the Syrian cult of Sol Invictus or the Persian cult of&#xd;\n44347\tMithras, Asia Minor deities and theologies were considerably favoured. Epigraphic and archaeological evidence confirms the existence of the cults of Magna Mater, Attis, Iuppiter Dolichenus, Sabazius, Iuppiter Turmasgades, Iuppiter Melanus, Men and Artemis of Ephesus. However, in the eastern parts of the Central Balkan Roman provinces, certain religious syncretism is emphasized, which can be connected to the strong Thracian influence in the mentioned territory. This paper examines the ways and the degree to which Thracian culture penetrated the religious beliefs and funerary rites of the population that inhabited the eastern parts of the Central Balkans in Antiquity.</dc:description>\n44348\t<dc:description>Bulletin of the national archaeological Institute XLIV</dc:description>\n44349\t<dc:date>2024-02-01T13:59:48Z</dc:date>"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d","uuid":"4f3f9e2a-5622-4864-bebe-b38e615a14f7","timestamp":"2026-10-25T22:07:16.637Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Svemir\\data\\sessions\\c1792946760393lb6a\\medijana_baza\\roj_glm\\objekti_CD\\oai_full.xml","content":"<dc:identifier>https://rai.ai.ac.rs/handle/123456789/1562</dc:identifier>\n<dc:identifier>http://rai.ai.ac.rs/bitstream/id/4640/bitstream_4640.pdf</dc:identifier>\n<dc:identifier>https://hdl.handle.net/21.15107/rcub_rai_1562</dc:identifier>\n<dc:language>en</dc:language>\n<dc:rights>openAccess</dc:rights>\n<dc:rights>ARR</dc:rights>\n<dc:publisher>Molina de Aragón: Junta de Comunidades de Castilla-La Mancha</dc:publisher>\n<dc:source>Celtic Religion across Space and Time: fontes epigraphici religionum celticarum antiquarum (IX Workshop F.E.R.C.AN. 17–20 de septiembre 2008)</dc:source>\n</oai_dc:dc></metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:rai.ai.ac.rs:123456789/1555</identifier><datestamp>2026-07-24T08:24:30Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_123456789_1</setSpec><setSpec>col_123456789_3</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/\" xmlns:doc=\"http://www.lyncode.com/xoai\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\" xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\" xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd\">\n<dc:title>Carska ideologija u arhitekturi, umetnosti i skulpturi rimske vile na Medijani</dc:title>\n<dc:creator>Milošević, Gordana</dc:creator>\n<dc:creator>Gavrilović, Nadežda</dc:creator>\n<dc:subject>Konstantin Veliki</dc:subject>\n<dc:subject>Naissus</dc:subject>\n<dc:subject>carska ideologija</dc:subject>\n<dc:subject>Medijana</dc:subject>\n<dc:description>U radu se raspravlja o novim tumacenjima rimske vile na suburbiumu Medijana. Na prostoru Medijane konstatovano i sistematski istraženo više gradevina razlicitih funkcija, kao što su na vila sa peristilom i termama, vila sa oktogonom, skladišta sa radionicama i vojnim barakama, dve ranohrišcanske bazilike, nekropole i više manjih vseoskih vila. Nova arheološka istraživanja vile sa peristilom sprovedenim u periodu od 2010 do 2012. godine omogucila su potpuno sagledavanje i izdvajanje graditeljskih faza, kao i analizu celokupne umetnosti kasnoantickog perioda zastupljenu u fresko-slikarstvu, mozaicima, arhitektonskoj plastici i skulpturi. Jasno je utvrdeno da se promene na vili sa peristilom u reprezentativni rezidencijalni objekat mogu vezati za period i graditeljske poduhvate Konstantina Velikog u Nišu.</dc:description>\n<dc:date>2024-02-01T11:44:44Z</dc:date>\n<dc:date>2024-02-01T11:44:44Z</dc:date>\n<dc:date>2013</dc:date>\n<dc:type>bookPart</dc:type>\n<dc:type>publishedVersion</dc:type>\n<dc:identifier>978-86-7148-176-2</dc:identifier>\n<dc:identifier>https://rai.ai.ac.rs/handle/123456789/1555</dc:identifier>\n<dc:identifier>http://rai.ai.ac.rs/bitstream/id/4442/bitstream_4442.pdf</dc:identifier>\n<dc:identifier>https://hdl.handle.net/21.15107/rcub_rai_1555</dc:identifier>\n<dc:language>sr</dc:language>\n<dc:relation>info:eu-repo/grantAgreement/MESTD/Basic Research (BR or ON)/177007/RS//</dc:relation>\n<dc:rights>openAccess</dc:rights>\n<dc:rights>ARR</dc:rights>\n<dc:publisher>Niš : Pravni fakultet Univerziteta u Nišu</dc:publisher>\n<dc:source>Zbornik radova 1700 godina Milanskog edikta</dc:source>\n</oai_dc:dc></metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:rai.ai.ac.rs:123456789/1563</identifier><datestamp>2026-05-07T10:24:07Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_123456789_1</setSpec><setSpec>col_123456789_3</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/\" xmlns:doc=\"http://www.lyncode.com/xoai\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\" xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\" xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd\">\n<dc:title>Thracian Influence in Asia Minor Mystery Cults in the Eastern Parts of the Roman Provinces in the Central Balkans</dc:title>\n<dc:creator>Gavrilović Vitas, Nadežda</dc:creator>\n<dc:subject>Asia Minor cults</dc:subject>\n<dc:subject>Central Balkans</dc:subject>\n<dc:subject>mistery religions</dc:subject>\n<dc:subject>funerary rites</dc:subject>\n<dc:subject>snake</dc:subject>\n<dc:description>During the period of Roman rule in the Central Balkan Roman provinces,&#xd;\namong other oriental cults, like the Syrian cult of Sol Invictus or the Persian cult of&#xd;\nMithras, Asia Minor deities and theologies were considerably favoured. Epigraphic and archaeological evidence confirms the existence of the cults of Magna Mater, Attis, Iuppiter Dolichenus, Sabazius, Iuppiter Turmasgades, Iuppiter Melanus, Men and Artemis of Ephesus. However, in the eastern parts of the Central Balkan Roman provinces, certain religious syncretism is emphasized, which can be connected to the strong Thracian influence in the mentioned territory. This paper examines the ways and the degree to which Thracian culture penetrated the religious beliefs and funerary rites of the population that inhabited the eastern parts of the Central Balkans in Antiquity.</dc:description>\n<dc:description>Bulletin of the national archaeological Institute XLIV</dc:description>\n<dc:date>2024-02-01T13:59:48Z</dc:date>","numLines":45,"startLine":44305,"totalLines":71039}}}
