{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261026060723332ef5ee2cb345d0","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Three works by Gordana Milošević in RAI:\n1. \"Excavations of Mediana in 2010 and 2011\" — Vasić, Miloje; Milošević, Gordana; Gavrilović, Nadežda — Archaeologia Bulgarica — line 3092.\n2. \"Constantine's Villa at Mediana\" — monograph 2016 (record 1539).\n3. \"Carska ideologija u arhitekturi, umetnosti i skulpturi rimske vile na Medijani\" — Milošević, Gordana; Gavrilović, Nadežda (record around 44314).\n\nNone is \"Urbanism and Architecture of the Imperial Domain at Mediana\". But \"Carska ideologija u arhitekturi...\" is thematically close. Let me see its full record (identifier, year, source).\n\nAlso let me check the full record of \"Excavations of Mediana in 2010 and 2011\" (identifiers, bitstream PDF?) and the record before 1539 (bitstream_4422, record 1538).\n\nAlso — importantly — the description in record 1539 mentions \"villa with peristyle, thermae and antique gate\" — the monograph covers the domain broadly. The Academia paper \"Urbanism and Architecture of the Imperial Domain at Mediana\" could actually be the English summary chapter of this monograph, or a standalone paper in the monograph \"Constantine's Villa at Mediana\" itself? The Academia upload date (ID 44911502, ~2020-2021) doesn't match 2016 monograph... but Academia users often upload old papers late. Or it could be a chapter in a different volume.\n\nLet me look at the details around lines 44309-44340 for the \"Carska ideologija\" record, and 3080-3130 for the Archaeologia Bulgarica paper (bitstream available?), and 43840-43878 for record 1538.","signature":"2c449052ead74aaaa110c515"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"call_58909c1e0d5f4aed9a483050","session_id":"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d","uuid":"55ee88a3-3225-4247-