{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_d27d14e06f234650b2219507","type":"tool_result","content":"3092\t<dc:title>Excavations of Mediana in 2010 and 2011</dc:title>\n3093\t<dc:creator>Vasić, Miloje</dc:creator>\n3094\t<dc:creator>Milošević, Gordana</dc:creator>\n3095\t<dc:creator>Gavrilović, Nadežda</dc:creator>\n3096\t<dc:subject>Medijana</dc:subject>\n3097\t<dc:subject>vila s peristilom</dc:subject>\n3098\t<dc:subject>stratigrafija</dc:subject>\n3099\t<dc:subject>arhitektura</dc:subject>\n3100\t<dc:subject>pokretni nalazi</dc:subject>\n3101\t<dc:subject>kasna antika</dc:subject>\n3102\t<dc:description>Throughout 2010 and 2011, a systematic nine month archaeological exploration\n3103\t   was conducted on the north-eastern, northwestern and south-eastern parts of\n3104\t   the villa with peristyle, as well as the area in front of the museum building\n3105\t   (see note 8). The envisaged area of exploration was around 1,400 m². In\n3106\t   total, 1,230 m² of this area was thoroughly examined (Fig. 1). The\n3107\t   excavations were performed with the aim of defining the dimensions of the\n3108\t   north-western and south-western parts of the villa, the appearance of the\n3109\t   villa’s entrance, as well as to explore the foundations of the museum\n3110\t   building. In the course of the excavations, certain differences were\n3111\t   perceived in the stratigraphy of the villa with peristyle and the part\n3112\t   excavated outside the villa.</dc:description>\n3113\t<dc:date>2022-05-10T11:23:58Z</dc:date>\n3114\t<dc:date>2022-05-10T11:23:58Z</dc:date>\n3115\t<dc:date>2014</dc:date>\n3116\t<dc:type>article</dc:type>\n3117\t<dc:type>publishedVersion</dc:type>\n3118\t<dc:identifier>0350-0241</dc:identifier>\n3119\t<dc:identifier>https://rai.ai.ac.rs/handle/123456789/210</dc:identifier>\n3120\t<dc:identifier>10.2298/STA1464231V</dc:identifier>\n3121\t<dc:identifier>http://rai.ai.ac.rs/bitstream/id/92/207.pdf</dc:identifier>\n3122\t<dc:rights>openAccess</dc:rights>\n3123\t<dc:rights>https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/</dc:rights>\n3124\t<dc:rights>BY-NC-ND</dc:rights>\n3125\t<dc:publisher>Arheološki institut, Beograd</dc:publisher>\n3126\t<dc:source>Starinar</dc:source>\n3127\t</oai_dc:dc></metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:rai.ai.ac.rs:123456789/211</identifier><datestamp>2022-05-10T11:24:03Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_123456789_1</setSpec><setSpec>col_123456789_3</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/\" xmlns:doc=\"http://www.lyncode.com/xoai\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\" xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\" xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd\">\n3128\t<dc:title>Corded Ware in the Central and Southern Balkans: A Consequence of Cultural Interaction or an Indication of Ethnic Change?</dc:title>\n3129\t<dc:creator>Bulatović, Aleksandar</dc:creator>\n3130\t<dc:description>The analysis of corded ware and accompanying artifacts reveals the nature of its appearance across the Central and Southern Balkan Eneolithic during three cultural-chronological horizons. The first horizon corresponds to the Early Eneolithic, namely the Bubanj-Salcuta-Krivodol cultural complex (BSK), while the second corresponds to the Cotofeni culture. The third horizon, showing chronological continuity with the second, and set within the Late Eneolithic/ Early Bronze Age, has a site distribution that encompasses the territory of nearly the entire Balkan Peninsula, where corded ware is found together with other steppe elements which are present in large numbers, such are burials under mounds and the appearance of the domestic horse.</dc:description>\n3131\t<dc:date>2022-05-10T11:24:03Z</dc:date>\n3132\t<dc:date>2022-05-10T11:24:03Z</dc:date>\n3133\t<dc:date>2014</dc:date>\n3134\t<dc:type>article</dc:type>\n3135\t<dc:type>publishedVersion</dc:type>\n3136\t<dc:identifier>0092-2323</dc:identifier>"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"call_58909c1e0d5f4aed9a483050","session_id":"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d","uuid":"1fa8ef64-393e-436b-8ed6-fc737314a695","timestamp":"2026-10-25T22:07:33.907Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Lov na Milošević Urbanism Mediana"}
