{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261026060722989f7158cd7c4ba1","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent finds:\n\n1. **Vasić, Milošević, Gavrilović Vitas, Crnoglavac 2016 — \"Constantine's Villa at Mediana\"** — THE MONOGRAPH (English edition, National Museum Niš, ISBN 978-86-83019-46-5), openAccess, PDF: http://rai.ai.ac.rs/bitstream/id/4423/bitstream_4423.pdf, handle 123456789/1539. This is the \"Vasić et al. 2016 monografija\" mentioned in aus2018 bibliography! It covers \"villa with peristyle, thermae and antique gate\" — thermae are relevant! This is a huge lead — the full monograph PDF is open access.\n\nWait — the base README says pdf/ has \"preuzeti PDF-ovi... (Starinar, Pop-Lazić, Gavrilović-Vitas i dr.)\" — maybe the monograph is already in the base's pdf/ folder? The base v0.14 mozaici_sloj references \"monografija\" (25 unosa mozaika, zbir 780,9 m², \"saglasno sa ~1000 m² monografije\"). The monograph might be already processed. But its OAI description mentions \"villa with peristyle, thermae and antique gate\" — thermae = potentially object with A-D labels? The A-D object labels — the geofizika sloj mentions \"istocni horeum, barake 8x4,5, vojni logor 160x160, apsidalni objekat\" from Starinar 61/2011 geomagnetic survey. Objects A/B/C/D...\n\nActually wait — in SINTEZA/README, the \"stibadium A\" and \"stibadium B\" are labeled A and B! From Starinar 64/2014 — stibadium A i B (garden fountains/dining pavilions). So \"objekat A\" and \"objekat B\" in the Drča 2000 sense... Hmm, but the task says \"objekat B\" (Drča 2000, Zbornik NMN 9, 21–36). And objects C and D \"van vile sa peristilom\". \n\nIn Starinar 64/2014 (which the base has), stibadium A and B are known. So Drča's \"objekat B\" might be stibadium B? And objekat C i D would be... other structures. Let me check what the base SINTEZA says about the A-D question — the summary says \"Otvoreno: osnova objekata C–D\".\n\n2. **Milošević & Gavrilović 2013 — \"Carska ideologija u arhitekturi, umetnosti i skulpturi rimske vile na Medijani\"** (Zbornik 1700 godina Milanskog edikta, Pravni fakultet Niš) — openAccess PDF http://rai.ai.ac.rs/bitstream/id/4442/bitstream_4442.pdf. Description mentions: \"vila sa peristilom i termama, vila sa oktogonom, skladišta sa radionicama i vojnim barakama, dve ranohrišćanske bazilike, nekropole i više manjih seoskih vila\" — this gives the full inventory of Mediana buildings! \"skladišta sa radionicama i vojnim barakama\" = the horreum/barracks (geomagnetic, Starinar 61/2011).\n\nSo the RAI OAI catalog has open-access PDFs I can download. The Milošević \"Urbanism and Architecture of the Imperial Domain at Mediana\" (Academia 44911502) — NOT found in RAI catalog (grep Urbanism gave nothing except unrelated). But wait — grep found no \"Urbanism\" at all in oai_full.xml. So RAI indeed doesn't have it. The 2013 bookPart + 2016 monograph are the closest open surrogates.\n\nNext moves:\n1. Check oai_all.xml and oai_2020.xml for more Mediana records (100 records only in oai_all — probably a subset; oai_2020 maybe date-filtered).\n2. Try downloading the two open-access PDFs via web_reader (rate-limited right now) or via curl? Shell is restrictive but curl might work as a single command. The pale session apparently downloaded files somehow (tapavicki pdf is on disk!). How did it download? Probably via Bash curl single commands. Let me check izvrsavanje.log for curl usage to confirm the working pattern.\n3. Also search the catalog for more: \"Mediana\" titles I haven't seen — the grep earlier gave hits at lines 241, 1756-1766, 4820, 20588, 28263, 29631 that I haven't read yet. Line 28263 and 20588 might be relevant. Let me read those.\n\nAlso line 3092 record I saw: Starinar 64/2014 with PDF http://rai.ai.ac.rs/bitstream/id/92/207.pdf — that's the article the base already decoded (crtezi_sloj). Good to confirm open PDF exists.\n\nLet me read remaining Mediana hits: 20588, 28263, 29631, 4820, 1756-1766, 241.","signature":"4a989021ae8e4cc5a62a9062"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d","uuid":"ea8b5564-ed08-4303-9ac9-9c7570b39a46","timestamp":"2026-10-25T22:07:39.017Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261026060722989f7158cd7c4ba1","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dva velika pogotka u katalogu: monografija „Constantine's Villa at Mediana\" (2016, openAccess PDF) i Milošević–Gavrilović 2013. Proveravam preostale Mediana zapise u katalogu:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d","uuid":"3c2c150c-1edf-40c9-81d1-b50c6a7038b0","timestamp":"2026-10-25T22:07:39.022Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261026060722989f7158cd7c4ba1","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_9f57162957294d58944bd367","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Svemir\\data\\sessions\\c1792946760393lb6a\\medijana_baza\\roj_glm\\objekti_CD\\oai_full.xml","limit":30,"offset":28250}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d","uuid":"186e7c56-e36e-44d3-af83-b05714cd6f2a","timestamp":"2026-10-25T22:07:39.857Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_9f57162957294d58944bd367","type":"tool_result","content":"28250\t<dc:publisher>Нови Сад : Матица српска</dc:publisher>\n28251\t<dc:source>Зборник Матице српске за класичне студије 20/2018, 2019, 392-393</dc:source>\n28252\t</oai_dc:dc></metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:rai.ai.ac.rs:123456789/953</identifier><datestamp>2024-04-29T10:10:26Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_123456789_1</setSpec><setSpec>col_123456789_3</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/\" xmlns:doc=\"http://www.lyncode.com/xoai\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\" xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\" xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd\">\n28253\t<dc:title>Late antique paintings in Naissus : Historical, social and archaeological context</dc:title>\n28254\t<dc:creator>Jeremić, Gordana</dc:creator>\n28255\t<dc:subject>Naissus</dc:subject>\n28256\t<dc:subject>wall paintings</dc:subject>\n28257\t<dc:subject>tombs</dc:subject>\n28258\t<dc:subject>urban structures</dc:subject>\n28259\t<dc:subject>villas</dc:subject>\n28260\t<dc:subject>motifs</dc:subject>\n28261\t<dc:subject>figural representations</dc:subject>\n28262\t<dc:subject>artistic workshops</dc:subject>\n28263\t<dc:description>The frescoes in public and private buildings testify to the importance of this kind of decoration in the Constantinian and post-Constantinian city of Naissus and its surroundings. Archaeological research established the fact that painted walls could be found in representative buildings within the Late Antique fortified city of Naissus and the economic-distributive centre with villas of rich citizens in the vicinity of the city, in the suburbium identified as Mediana. &#xd;\n28264\tThe problem regarding the workshops which made the frescos in the 4th century and later periods remains open since parallels can be found in a wider Balkans region, but also in important cultural centres of the eastern and western provinces of the Roman Empire.</dc:description>\n28265\t<dc:date>2023-11-23T11:57:56Z</dc:date>\n28266\t<dc:date>2023-11-23T11:57:56Z</dc:date>\n28267\t<dc:date>2019</dc:date>\n28268\t<dc:type>conferenceObject</dc:type>\n28269\t<dc:type>publishedVersion</dc:type>\n28270\t<dc:identifier>https://disci.unibo.it/it/eventi/pareti-dipinte-scavo-valorizzazione-XIV-colloquio-aipma-2019</dc:identifier>\n28271\t<dc:identifier>https://rai.ai.ac.rs/handle/123456789/953</dc:identifier>\n28272\t<dc:identifier>http://rai.ai.ac.rs/bitstream/id/2164/14_PREATTI_2019_Late_antique_paintings_in_Naissus.pdf</dc:identifier>\n28273\t<dc:identifier>https://hdl.handle.net/21.15107/rcub_rai_953</dc:identifier>\n28274\t<dc:language>en</dc:language>\n28275\t<dc:relation>info:eu-repo/grantAgreement/MESTD/Basic Research (BR or ON)/177007/RS//</dc:relation>\n28276\t<dc:rights>openAccess</dc:rights>\n28277\t<dc:rights>https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/</dc:rights>\n28278\t<dc:rights>ARR</dc:rights>\n28279\t<dc:publisher>Napoli : Museo Nazionale di Napoli; Bologna: Università di Bologna</dc:publisher>"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d","uuid":"c26d5c35-2ca3-4bdc-8614-3014aa449af9","timestamp":"2026-10-25T22:07:39.876Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Svemir\\data\\sessions\\c1792946760393lb6a\\medijana_baza\\roj_glm\\objekti_CD\\oai_full.xml","content":"<dc:publisher>Нови Сад : Матица српска</dc:publisher>\n<dc:source>Зборник Матице српске за класичне студије 20/2018, 2019, 392-393</dc:source>\n</oai_dc:dc></metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:rai.ai.ac.rs:123456789/953</identifier><datestamp>2024-04-29T10:10:26Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_123456789_1</setSpec><setSpec>col_123456789_3</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/\" xmlns:doc=\"http://www.lyncode.com/xoai\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\" xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\" xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd\">\n<dc:title>Late antique paintings in Naissus : Historical, social and archaeological context</dc:title>\n<dc:creator>Jeremić, Gordana</dc:creator>\n<dc:subject>Naissus</dc:subject>\n<dc:subject>wall paintings</dc:subject>\n<dc:subject>tombs</dc:subject>\n<dc:subject>urban structures</dc:subject>\n<dc:subject>villas</dc:subject>\n<dc:subject>motifs</dc:subject>\n<dc:subject>figural representations</dc:subject>\n<dc:subject>artistic workshops</dc:subject>\n<dc:description>The frescoes in public and private buildings testify to the importance of this kind of decoration in the Constantinian and post-Constantinian city of Naissus and its surroundings. Archaeological research established the fact that painted walls could be found in representative buildings within the Late Antique fortified city of Naissus and the economic-distributive centre with villas of rich citizens in the vicinity of the city, in the suburbium identified as Mediana. &#xd;\nThe problem regarding the workshops which made the frescos in the 4th century and later periods remains open since parallels can be found in a wider Balkans region, but also in important cultural centres of the eastern and western provinces of the Roman Empire.</dc:description>\n<dc:date>2023-11-23T11:57:56Z</dc:date>\n<dc:date>2023-11-23T11:57:56Z</dc:date>\n<dc:date>2019</dc:date>\n<dc:type>conferenceObject</dc:type>\n<dc:type>publishedVersion</dc:type>\n<dc:identifier>https://disci.unibo.it/it/eventi/pareti-dipinte-scavo-valorizzazione-XIV-colloquio-aipma-2019</dc:identifier>\n<dc:identifier>https://rai.ai.ac.rs/handle/123456789/953</dc:identifier>\n<dc:identifier>http://rai.ai.ac.rs/bitstream/id/2164/14_PREATTI_2019_Late_antique_paintings_in_Naissus.pdf</dc:identifier>\n<dc:identifier>https://hdl.handle.net/21.15107/rcub_rai_953</dc:identifier>\n<dc:language>en</dc:language>\n<dc:relation>info:eu-repo/grantAgreement/MESTD/Basic Research (BR or ON)/177007/RS//</dc:relation>\n<dc:rights>openAccess</dc:rights>\n<dc:rights>https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/</dc:rights>\n<dc:rights>ARR</dc:rights>\n<dc:publisher>Napoli : Museo Nazionale di Napoli; Bologna: Università di Bologna</dc:publisher>","numLines":30,"startLine":28250,"totalLines":71039}}}
