{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_394132fe0ce147c0ac194367","type":"tool_result","content":"29418\t<dc:identifier>https://hdl.handle.net/21.15107/rcub_rai_977</dc:identifier>\n29419\t<dc:language>sr</dc:language>\n29420\t<dc:relation>info:eu-repo/grantAgreement/MESTD/Basic Research (BR or ON)/177007/RS//</dc:relation>\n29421\t<dc:rights>openAccess</dc:rights>\n29422\t<dc:rights>ARR</dc:rights>\n29423\t<dc:publisher>Београд : Дрштво за античке студије Србије</dc:publisher>\n29424\t<dc:source>Антика некад и сад: значај, улога и наслеђе кроз векове. 11. Међународни научни скуп, 16-17. децембар 2017, Књига резимеа</dc:source>\n29425\t</oai_dc:dc></metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:rai.ai.ac.rs:123456789/978</identifier><datestamp>2025-06-12T11:26:00Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_123456789_1</setSpec><setSpec>col_123456789_3</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/\" xmlns:doc=\"http://www.lyncode.com/xoai\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\" xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\" xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd\">\n29426\t<dc:title>Representation of Medusa on a mosaic floor in Mediana</dc:title>\n29427\t<dc:creator>Jeremić, Gordana</dc:creator>\n29428\t<dc:contributor>Vujović, Miroslav B.</dc:contributor>\n29429\t<dc:subject>Mediana / villa with peristyle / aula / floor mosaic / Medusa / late antiquity / 4th century</dc:subject>\n29430\t<dc:description>A number of representative rooms decorated by mosaic floors from the period around the 4th century were examined during the archaeological research of the villa with peristyle in the middle of the late antiquity settlement in Mediana near Naissus. In 1969, a part of the damaged mosaic floor with geometrical motifs and a central round emblem including a representation of Medusa-Gorgon with wings was discovered in the central room of the villa, that is, in a large triclinium-aula. Medusa is represented in the manner of late antiquity, as a woman with a pensive expression who has lost many of the attributes characteristic of such representations in Greek and Hellenistic art. The aim of this paper is not only to provide analyses of the visual artistic aspect of the presentation but also to attempt a reconstruction of the mosaic carpet in the room on the basis of various site data, which are now available to researchers.</dc:description>\n29431\t<dc:date>2023-11-23T12:24:59Z</dc:date>\n29432\t<dc:date>2023-11-23T12:24:59Z</dc:date>\n29433\t<dc:date>2017</dc:date>\n29434\t<dc:type>bookPart</dc:type>\n29435\t<dc:type>publishedVersion</dc:type>\n29436\t<dc:identifier>978-86-6427-068-7</dc:identifier>\n29437\t<dc:identifier>https://rai.ai.ac.rs/handle/123456789/978</dc:identifier>\n29438\t<dc:identifier>http://rai.ai.ac.rs/bitstream/id/2209/05_ANTE_PORTAM_AUREAM_2017_Representation_of_Medusa_on_a_mosaic_floor.pdf</dc:identifier>\n29439\t<dc:identifier>https://hdl.handle.net/21.15107/rcub_rai_978</dc:identifier>\n29440\t<dc:language>en</dc:language>\n29441\t<dc:relation>info:eu-repo/grantAgreement/MESTD/Basic Research (BR or ON)/177007/RS//</dc:relation>\n29442\t<dc:rights>openAccess</dc:rights>"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"call_228a9101adba430ca741f6e2","session_id":"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d","uuid":"9972fb32-682e-4cf5-b9b9-6b6997ea8239","timestamp":"2026-10-25T22:07:44.456Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Lov na Jeremić 2006 mozaici"}
