{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_2026102606090092127a9460594671","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK — ZADATAK confirms the framing. Objects C-D are buildings of the complex outside the villa. The A-D lettering system most plausibly comes from the Petrović 1994 monograph's situational plan (P. Petrović, \"Medijana\", Archaeologia Iugoslavica / Niš 1994?) — where buildings around the villa got letters. The geofizika sloj from Starinar 61/2011 lists structures 1-16. The base has 19 stubova with names.\n\nWhat could A-D be? From literature knowledge of Mediana:\n- The villa with peristile (central)\n- Thermae (west of villa)\n- The \"villa with octagon\" (south, near the Nišava)\n- Granary/horreum + barracks (east, from geomagnetics)\n- Two early Christian basilicas (church 1 and 2)\n- The water tower/castellum aquae\n- The gate\n\nIn Petrović's monograph and older plans, buildings are marked... Actually in some Mediana literature, \"object A\" and \"object B\" refer to the two villa-like buildings: \"vila sa peristilom\" = hotel/museum area... Hmm.\n\nDrča 2000 in Zbornik Narodnog muzeja Niš 9, 21–36: \"objekat B\" — I recall from the summary: Drča Slobodan, \"Mediana — objekat B\" possibly the thermae? Or the building NW of the villa?\n\nI can't resolve this from memory — need sources. The monograph \"Constantine's Villa at Mediana\" 2016 (openAccess PDF!) is the strongest document to resolve the A-D system AND provide measures for the outer buildings. Priority #1 download.\n\nAlso Petrović 1994 monograph — Cyrillic reference in FASTI bibliography (\"Медијана\" monograph 1994, unreadable OCR). The 2016 monograph likely cites it.\n\nNow retry web_reader (a few minutes passed). Try on the monograph PDF bitstream URL. web_reader return_format text — it may extract PDF text via their server. Try:\nhttp://rai.ai.ac.rs/bitstream/id/4423/bitstream_4423.pdf\n\nIf PDF extraction unsupported, try the handle