e (Fig 2, 5!). Fig. 2 legend: 1. corridors; 1. podium (numbering glitch); 2. aula; 3. eastern triclinium; 4. western triclinium; 5. corridor which connected the villa with the thermae.\n\n- Six buildings with mosaics: five residential + one early Christian church ( 2006, 145-157 = Jeremić 2006! \"G. Jeremić 2006\" the mosaics monograph chapter in Niš i Vizantija 4; and \" 2010, 98-99\" = her doctoral dissertation 2010).\n\nSo Jeremić 2006 = \"( 2006, 145-157)\" — confirmed: chapter/pages 145-157, likely in \"Ниш и Византија 4\" (Niš and Byzantium 4, 2006?). The citation \"Vasić 2006, 69\" is M. Vasić 2006.\n\nNow let me read the rest of the Meduza paper (bibliography) to get exact refs. The file is 37 KB; I read to line 160. Read the remainder — especially the reference list, which will resolve: 1994 monograph author (Petroushko? no — it's Петровић), 2013 work identity, 2006 identity.","signature":"e58d609104b8427983cea869"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d","uuid":"2b7bd826-7282-424b-8f7d-a6d1b1ae70cb","timestamp":"2026-10-25T22:09:32.074Z"}
