{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261026060932f8b2abc654564453","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The Meduza 2017 bibliography is GOLD — it resolves several key citations:\n\n1. **Petrović 1994 confirmed**: „P. Petrović, Medijana. Rezidencija rimskih careva, Beograd 1994\" — the monograph (P. Петровић, Медијана. Резиденција римских царева). The FASTI Cyrillic 1994 reference is THIS.\n2. **Jeremić 2006 confirmed**: „G. Jeremić, Mozaici Medijane — neka razmatranja, u: Niš i Vizantija IV, Četvrti naučni skup, Niš 3.–5. jun 2005, Niš 2006, 145–158.\" (the OCR said 145-157 in text, bibliography says 145-158 — minor discrepancy).\n3. **Milošević 2013**: „G. Milošević, Arhitektura rezidencijalnog kompleksa na Medijani, u: Konstantin Veliki i Milanski edikt 313. Rađanje hrišćanstva u rimskim provincijama na tlu Srbije, I. Popović, B. Borić-Bresković (ur.), Beograd 2013, 118–125.\" — WAIT. This is DIFFERENT from the RAI 2013 bookPart (Carska ideologija u arhitekturi... Zbornik 1700 godina Milanskog edikta, Pravni fakultet Niš). Two different 2013 publications! The one cited in Meduza (aerial photo p. 51, villa plan p. 53, mosaic surfaces 121-124, settlement 80 ha p. 93?) — hmm wait, \"( 2013, 93)\" = Milošević 2013, 93 — but the article is 118-125? No — page 93 citation must be from Vasić 2013 (76-101). Both 2013 works exist:\n   - Milošević 2013: \"Arhitektura rezidencijalnog kompleksa na Medijani\", in Konstantin Veliki i Milanski edikt 313 (SANU/Srpska književna zadruga? Belgrade 2013), pp. 118-125 — this has Fig. aerial photo (p. 51?) no wait, the article spans 118-125, so \" 2013, . 51\" (Fig. 1 after p. 51) can't be Milošević... Actually Fig 1 \"after:  2013, . 51\" — hmm, could be ВАСИЋ 2013 (76-101)? No, p. 51 outside range too. Could be \"Милошевић 2013\" in a different publication... The Jeremić 2006/2010 cites are clear. The Cyrillic-only author names got OCR-stripped. Fig. 2 \"after:  2013, . 53\" — same 2013 work with plans at pp. 51 and 53. But Milošević's article in the citation above is 118-125 — pp. 51/53 fall in VASIĆ 2013 (76-101)? No. Neither.\n   \n   Hmm — actually maybe there are TWO Milošević 2013 entries in the bibliography. I only see one Cyrillic 2013 for Milošević (118-125) and one for Vasić (76-101). Pages 51 and 53 fall outside both... unless the citation \"( 2013, . 51)\" refers to a THIRD 2013 item not in bibliography (oversight), OR the OCR garbled page numbers (e.g., 151, 153 — which would fall inside... no). Or Fig.1/2 after \"Милошеви 2013\" where the actual publication is her Fig at pp. 51, 53 of ANOTHER work — the \"Carska ideologija\" from Pravni fakultet Niš 2013! That's likely: G. Milošević, \"Carska ideologija u arhitekturi, umetnosti i skulpturi rimske vile na Medijani\", Zbornik radova 1700 godina Milanskog edikta, Niš 2013 — could have the aerial photo and mosaic-surface plan at pp. 51/53! And the OCR of the bibliography in Meduza paper might have missed a second Milošević 2013 entry, OR the Meduza bibliography lists only one and the figs cite the Niš one sloppily. Either way — the RAI-hosted \"Carska ideologija...\" (bitstream_4442) is a top download target; it likely contains the mosaic-surface plan (Fig. 2 of Meduza = \"after Milošević 2013\") and architecture summary.\n\n4. **Vasić 2007**: \"Mediana — eine kaiserliche Villa bei Niš\", in: U. Brandl, M. Vasić, \"Roms Erbe auf dem Balkan. Spätantike Kaiservillen und Stadtanlagen in Serbien\", Mainz am Rhein 2007, 96–197 — a 100-page German treatment! That's the big synthetic work. (Probably not open access; von Zabern.)\n5. Vasić 2005 (Mediana - domaine impérial ou bien privé?, 167-176), Vasić 2006 (Stibadium in Romuliana and Mediana, 69-75), Zotović-Petrović 1969 (Arheološki pregled 11, 185-186), Bratanich 1938 (Starinar XIII, 199-204).\n\nAlso NEW HARD MEASURE for mera.json: **aula 19.6 × 12 m, apse depth 5.2 m; square carpet 5.5 × 5.5 m; octagon 2.8 m; medallion 0.8 m; lateral carpets width 2.4 m; room length 19.6 m** — but note: aula is INSIDE the villa (base probably has it). Still valuable cross-check for mozaici_sloj (base v0.14 says aula Meduza; surface numbers may match).\n\nAlso footnote [2]: \"horreum, military barracks and villa with peristyle may have been built around 330\" — the horreum and military barracks (from geofizika sloj: istočni horeum, barake 8×4,5 m, vojni logor 160×160 m). These ARE the objects outside the villa! Could \"objekat C\" and \"objekat D\" be...? Still unknown labeling.\n\nNow the top-priority download list:\n1. bitstream_4423.pdf — Constantine's Villa at Mediana monograph 2016 (RAI, openAccess)\n2. bitstream_4442.pdf — Milošević \"Carska ideologija...\" Niš 2013 (RAI, openAccess)\n3. Starinar 66/2016 stibadium B article (handle 254) — bitstream id? From record 4812 area: the record before (handle 253) had bitstream id/122/250.pdf; stibadium B is handle 254 — need its bitstream URL (record after 4820; read lines 4829-4860).\n4. Vasić 2013 \"Gradovi i carske vile...\" (Konstantin Veliki i Milanski edikt 313, 76-101) — maybe also on RAI? grep oai_full for \"Milanski edikt\".\n\nLet me grep the catalog for \"Milanski\" and read handle 254's bitstream.","signature":"699ef48ccb864254aa395582"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d","uuid":"354b69c0-48c6-4aaa-aa5a-023d2e510afb","timestamp":"2026-10-25T22:09:56.855Z"}
