{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_62ad3c59156c4268bb16b475","type":"tool_result","content":"3851-   the inner courtyard. Rooms I, J and K had floor and wall heating, while rooms\n3852-   G and H had an arched apse and possibly functioned as a reception hall and/or\n3853:   a stibadium. The hallway with mosaics, which flanks the inner courtyard, was\n3854-   most likely roofed. Traces of burning in the north-western corridor testify\n3855-   to the destruction of the building in a fire. Based on the architectural\n--\n4818-<dc:source>Starinar</dc:source>\n4819-[Omitted long context line]\n4820:<dc:title>Stibadium B of villa with peristyle at Mediana</dc:title>\n4821-<dc:creator>Gavrilović-Vitas, Nadežda</dc:creator>\n4822-<dc:creator>Milošević-Jevtić, Gordana</dc:creator>\n--\n4825-   2010 and 2011, a room of circular plan in the north-western segment of the\n4826-   villa and to the north of room w-24, was discovered. The room had annexes in\n4827:   the east and west and is analogous to the stibadium A discovered in the\n4828-   north-eastern section of the villa. Further investigations of the room called\n4829:   stibadium B revealed that the stibadium walls were decorated with a facing of\n4830-   marble slabs and the floor was covered with exceptionally well preserved high\n4831-   quality mosaic. Archaeological excavations in 2015 defined completely the\n4832:   system of floor and wall heating. The mosaic floors in stibadium B are\n4833:   conserved. The area to the west of the stibadium has also been explored and a\n4834-   channel with the remains of a lead water pipe was discovered there. The\n4835-   terrain to the north of the northern wall of the villa with peristyle was\n--\n59019-<dc:source>Starinar</dc:source>\n59020-[Omitted long context line]\n59021:<dc:title>Uncovering the Function of the Late antique building in Gornje Nerodimlje - From a stibadium, through a triclinium, to a villa rustica</dc:title>\n59022-<d