"output_tokens_details\":{\"thinking_tokens\":0},\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"stop_details\":null},\"attributionAgent\":\"general-purpose\",\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"6dd514bb-4a33-4234-842a-99a134437a46\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-25T22:07:07.426Z\",\"effort\":\"high\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"sdk-cli\",\"cwd\":\"C:\\\\Svemir\\\\data\\\\sessions\\\\c1792946760393lb6a\\\\medijana_baza\\\\roj_glm\\\\objekti_CD\",\"sessionId\":\"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d\",\"version\":\"2.1.232\",\"gitBranch\":\"master\",\"slug\":\"cached-soaring-sedgewick\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"6dd514bb-4a33-4234-842a-99a134437a46\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"promptId\":\"8f7a7d2d-dfff-49d8-9afd-b83bde684221\",\"agentId\":\"a7308cdff85b75b5c\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"call_3a656e58bf9c468fa9e78e5c\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"43870\\t<dc:identifier>https://rai.ai.ac.rs/handle/123456789/1538</dc:identifier>\\n43871\\t<dc:identifier>http://rai.ai.ac.rs/bitstream/id/4422/bitstream_4422.pdf</dc:identifier>\\n43872\\t<dc:identifier>https://hdl.handle.net/21.15107/rcub_rai_1538</dc:identifier>\\n43873\\t<dc:language>sr</dc:language>\\n43874\\t<dc:relation>info:eu-repo/grantAgreement/MESTD/Basic Research (BR or ON)/177007/RS//</dc:relation>\\n43875\\t<dc:rights>openAccess</dc:rights>\\n43876\\t<dc:rights>ARR</dc:rights>\\n43877\\t<dc:publisher>Beograd : Arheološki institut</dc:publisher>\\n43878\\t</oai_dc:dc></metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:rai.ai.ac.rs:123456789/1539</identifier><datestamp>2026-07-24T08:24:30Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_123456789_1</setSpec><setSpec>col_123456789_3</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc=\\\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/\\\" xmlns:doc=\\\"http://www.lyncode.com/xoai\\\" xmlns:xsi=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\\\" xmlns:dc=\\\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\\\" xsi:schemaLocation=\\\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd\\\">\\n43879\\t<dc:title>Constantine's Villa at Mediana</dc:title>\\n43880\\t<dc:creator>Vasić, Miloje</dc:creator>\\n43881\\t<dc:creator>Milošević, Gordana</dc:creator>\\n43882\\t<dc:creator>Gavrilović Vitas, Nadežda</dc:creator>\\n43883\\t<dc:creator>Crnoglavac, Vesna</dc:creator>\\n43884\\t<dc:subject>Villa with peristyle</dc:subject>\\n43885\\t<dc:subject>Constantine the Great</dc:subject>\\n43886\\t<dc:subject>Naissus</dc:subject>\\n43887\\t<dc:subject>IV century</dc:subject>\\n43888\\t<dc:subject>palatial complex</dc:subject>\\n43889\\t<dc:description>Constantine's Villa at Mediana is a monography about the administrative-residential complex of Roman emperor Constantine the Great at Mediana in Niš (antique Naissus). The monograph is based on the newest archaeological results of excavations and research conducted in the area of a large villa with peristyle, thermae and antique gate.</dc:description>\\n43890\\t<dc:date>2024-01-31T09:56:37Z</dc:date>\\n43891\\t<dc:date>2024-01-31T09:56:37Z</dc:date>\\n43892\\t<dc:date>2016</dc:date>\\n43893\\t<dc:type>book</dc:type>\\n43894\\t<dc:type>publishedVersion</dc:type>\\n43895\\t<dc:identifier>978-86-83019-46-5</dc:identifier>\\n43896\\t<dc:identifier>https://rai.ai.ac.rs/handle/123456789/1539</dc:identifier>\\n43897\\t<dc:identifier>http://rai.ai.ac.rs/bitstream/id/4423/bitstream_4423.pdf</dc:identifier>\\n43898\\t<dc:identifier>https://hdl.handle.net/21.15107/rcub_rai_1539</dc:identifier>\\n43899\\t<dc:language>en</dc:language>\\n43900\\t<dc:relation>Constantine’s villa at Mediana, financed by the Ministry of Culture and Information of Republic Serbia, no. 451-04-2024/2015-02</dc:relation>\\n43901\\t<dc:relation>info:eu-repo/grantAgreement/MESTD/Basic Research (BR or ON)/177007/RS//</dc:relation>\\n43902\\t<dc:rights>openAccess</dc:rights>\\n43903\\t<dc:rights>ARR</dc:rights>\\n43904\\t<dc:publisher>Niš: The National Museum Niš</dc:publisher>\\n43905\\t</oai_dc:dc></metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:rai.ai.ac.rs:123456789/1540</identifier><datestamp>2026-05-07T10:24:07Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_123456789_1</setSpec><setSpec>col_123456789_3</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc=\\\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/\\\" xmlns:doc=\\\"http://www.lyncode.com/xoai\\\" xmlns:xsi=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\\\" xmlns:dc=\\\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\\\" xsi:schemaLocation=\\\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd\\\">\\n43906\\t<dc:title>Ex Asia et Syria : Oriental Religions in the Roman Central Balkans</dc:title>\\n43907\\t<dc:creator>Gavrilović Vitas, Nadežda</dc:creator>\\n43908\\t<dc:subject>Asia Minor</dc:subject>\\n43909\\t<dc:subject>Syria</dc:subject>\\n43910\\t<dc:subject>Oriental cults</dc:subject>\\n43911\\t<dc:subject>Roman Central Balkans</dc:subject>\\n43912\\t<dc:description>The monograph \\\"Ex Asia Minor et Syria. Religions in the Roman Central Balkans\\\" investigates the cults of Asia Minor and Syrian origin in the Roman provinces of the Central Balkans. The author presents, analyzes and interprets all hitherto known epigraphical and archaeological material which attests to the presence of Asia Minor and Syrian cults in that region, a subject which is yet to be the object of a serious scholarly study. Thus the book both reviews previously known monuments and artefacts, many of which are now missing or are destroyed, and adds new finds, exploring their social and geographical context from all possible angles, and focusing on the thoughts and beliefs of the dedicators and devotees of the particular cult in question. New conclusions are presented in a scientific framework, taking account of the latest theoretical developments.</dc:description>\\n43913\\t<dc:description>Archaeopress Roman Archaeology, vol. 78.</dc:description>\\n43914\\t<dc:date>2024-01-31T10:06:33Z</dc:date>\\n43915\\t<dc:date>2024-01-31T10:06:33Z</dc:date>\\n43916\\t<dc:date>2021</dc:date>\\n43917\\t<dc:type>book</dc:type>\\n43918\\t<dc:type>publishedVersion</dc:type>\\n43919\\t<dc:identifier>978-1-78969-913-5</dc:identifier>\\n43920\\t<dc:identifier>https://rai.ai.ac.rs/handle/123456789/1540</dc:identifier>\\n43921\\t<dc:identifier>https://hdl.handle.net/21.15107/rcub_rai_1540</dc:identifier>\\n43922\\t<dc:language>en</dc:language>\\n43923\\t<dc:rights>restrictedAccess</dc:rights>\\n43924\\t<dc:rights>ARR</dc:rights>\\n43925\\t<dc:publisher>Archaeopress Publishing Ltd. Oxford</dc:publisher>\\n43926\\t</oai_dc:dc></metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:rai.ai.ac.rs:123456789/1541</identifier><datestamp>2026-05-07T10:24:07Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_123456789_1</setSpec><setSpec>col_123456789_3</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc=\\\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/\\\" xmlns:doc=\\\"http://www.lyncode.com/xoai\\\" xmlns:xsi=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\\\" xmlns:dc=\\\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\\\" xsi:schemaLocation=\\\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd\\\">\\n43927\\t<dc:title>Zeus and Hera Souideptenoi: The Sanctuary at Belava Mountain near Turres/Pirot</dc:title>\\n43928\\t<dc:creator>Gavrilović Vitas, Nadežda</dc:creator>\\n43929\\t<dc:creator>Dan, Dana</dc:creator>\\n43930\\t<dc:subject>Greek epigraphy</dc:subject>\\n43931\\t<dc:subject>Hera</dc:subject>\\n43932\\t<dc:subject>iconography</dc:subject>\\n43933\\t<dc:subject>Pirot (Turres)</dc:subject>\\n43934\\t<dc:subject>sanctuary</dc:subject>\\n43935\\t<dc:subject>Thrace</dc:subject>\\n43936\\t<dc:subject>votive icons</dc:subject>\\n43937\\t<dc:subject>Zeus</dc:subject>\\n43938\\t<dc:description>In the border zone between the Roman provinces of Upper Moesia and Thrace a sanctuary dedicated to Zeus and Hera, defined by the toponymic epithet Souideptenoi, was discovered on the Belava mountain, near Turres (today’s Pirot). The sanctuary presumably encompassed a temenos, an altar and two smaller temples, oriented east-west, with the entrance on the eastern side.&#xd;\\n43939\\tUnfortunately, illegal excavations were conducted on the area of the sanctuary by thieves, who stole the small reliefs offered to the deities venerated in the sanctuary, of which the authors of this paper could obtain the data of 31 fragmented votive plates, most of them inscribed. A variety of iconographic schemas, especially the standing divine couple or Zeus and Hera in quadriga,&#xd;\\n43940\\tas well as the combination of three onomastics stocks (Thracian, Greek and Latin) illustrate the diversity of traditions and the cultural interferences at work during imperial times. It can be presumed that the sanctuary dedicated to Zeus and Hera Souideptenoi existed from the 2nd to the end of the 3rd or the beginning of the 4th century.</dc:description>\\n43941\\t<dc:date>2024-01-31T10:33:27Z</dc:date>\\n43942\\t<dc:date>2024-01-31T10:33:27Z</dc:date>\\n43943\\t<dc:date>2022</dc:date>\\n43944\\t<dc:type>article</dc:type>\"}]},\"uuid\":\"f31a7c97-af04-4b21-9acd-4b746996a168\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-25T22:07:07.448Z\",\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"6dd514bb-4a33-4234-842a-99a134437a46\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"sdk-cli\",\"cwd\":\"C:\\\\Svemir\\\\data\\\\sessions\\\\c1792946760393lb6a\\\\medijana_baza\\\\roj_glm\\\\objekti_CD\",\"sessionId\":\"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d\",\"version\":\"2.1.232\",\"gitBranch\":\"master\",\"slug\":\"cached-soaring-sedgewick\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"f31a7c97-af04-4b21-9acd-4b746996a168\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a7308cdff85b75b5c\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"msg_202610260607087062bf4325524abb\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"MAJOR FIND: RAI record 123456789/1539 — \\\"Constantine's Villa at Mediana\\\", creators: Vasić, Miloje; Milošević, Gordana; Gavrilović Vitas, Nadežda; Crnoglavac, Vesna. 2016, book/monograph, ISBN 978-86-83019-46-5, publisher: Niš: The National Museum Niš, openAccess, PDF at http://rai.ai.ac.rs/bitstream/id/4423/bitstream_4423.pdf, handle https://rai.ai.ac.rs/handle/123456789/1539.\\n\\nThis confirms:\\n1. \\\"G. Milošević\\\" = **Gordana Milošević** (the name question from the task: Gordana, not Goran).\\n2. There's an open-access monograph \\\"Constantine's Villa at Mediana\\\" (2016, National Museum Niš) co-authored by Gordana Milošević — full PDF openly available! This may well contain the same content as the elusive \\\"Urbanism and Architecture of the Imperial Domain at Mediana\\\" paper (or at least the data sought: measures, positions, chronology).\\n\\nNote the Academia paper \\\"Urbanism and Architecture of the Imperial Domain at Mediana\\\" — 44911502 — uploaded ~2020-2021. Given the 2016 monograph, the Academia paper could be a chapter within the monograph or a separate conference paper. Actually — thinking about it — \\\"Urbanism and Architecture of the Imperial Domain at Mediana\\\" might be a chapter by Milošević in some English-language volume. But regardless, the open-access monograph PDF is the highest-value target now.\\n\\nAlso record 1538 (just above): identifier bitstream_4422.pdf — what was it? Line 43870-43877 shows the tail of record 1538: openAccess, Beograd: Arheološki institut. Let me check what 1538 is (title above line 43870). And also look for other works by Milošević, Gordana in the OAI harvest (grep \\\"Milošević, Gordana\\\").\\n\\nAlso worth checking \\\"The Latest Archaeological Discoveries about the Mediana Mosaics\\\" (line 45786).\\n\\nNext steps:\\n1. Grep oai_full.xml for \\\"Milošević, Gordana\\\" — list all her works in RAI.\\n2. Try to fetch the monograph PDF — but webReader is rate-limited and Bash/WebFetch denied. Hmm. I can try webReader again — some time has passed. If it works, fetch https://rai.ai.ac.rs/bitstream/id/4423/bitstream_4423.pdf — webReader on a PDF URL may not parse. Better fetch the handle page https://rai.ai.ac.rs/handle/123456789/1539 for metadata confirmation.\\n\\nLet me first grep for Milošević in oai_full.xml.\",\"signature\":\"ff6a5c9a4e5046b3b44c072f\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":0}},\"attributionAgent\":\"general-purpose\",\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"1b44db9f-33f4-4ecf-b43d-d296fbecc582\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-25T22:07:16.934Z\",\"effort\":\"high\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"sdk-cli\",\"cwd\":\"C:\\\\Svemir\\\\data\\\\sessions\\\\c1792946760393lb6a\\\\medijana_baza\\\\roj_glm\\\\objekti_CD\",\"sessionId\":\"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d\",\"version\":\"2.1.232\",\"gitBranch\":\"master\",\"slug\":\"cached-soaring-sedgewick\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"1b44db9f-33f4-4ecf-b43d-d296fbecc582\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a7308cdff85b75b5c\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"msg_202610260607087062bf4325524abb\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"KLJUČNI NALAZ: RAI 123456789/1539 — monografija \\\"Constantine's Villa at Mediana\\\" (2016, Narodni muzej Niš, ISBN 978-86-83019-46-5), autori: Miloje Vasić, **Gordana Milošević**, Nadežda Gavrilović Vitas, Vesna Crnoglavac — openAccess sa PDF-om! Ime je potvrđeno: Gordana. Tražim sve njene radove u harvestu.\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":0}},\"attributionAgent\":\"general-purpose\",\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"03fb62c4-03c6-4754-9e04-4cb466577ef0\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-25T22:07:18.148Z\",\"effort\":\"high\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"sdk-cli\",\"cwd\":\"C:\\\\Svemir\\\\data\\\\sessions\\\\c179294676039