aeologia Bulgarica — line 3092.\\n2. \\\"Constantine's Villa at Mediana\\\" — monograph 2016 (record 1539).\\n3. \\\"Carska ideologija u arhitekturi, umetnosti i skulpturi rimske vile na Medijani\\\" — Milošević, Gordana; Gavrilović, Nadežda (record around 44314).\\n\\nNone is \\\"Urbanism and Architecture of the Imperial Domain at Mediana\\\". But \\\"Carska ideologija u arhitekturi...\\\" is thematically close. Let me see its full record (identifier, year, source).\\n\\nAlso let me check the full record of \\\"Excavations of Mediana in 2010 and 2011\\\" (identifiers, bitstream PDF?) and the record before 1539 (bitstream_4422, record 1538).\\n\\nAlso — importantly — the description in record 1539 mentions \\\"villa with peristyle, thermae and antique gate\\\" — the monograph covers the domain broadly. The Academia paper \\\"Urbanism and Architecture of the Imperial Domain at Mediana\\\" could actually be the English summary chapter of this monograph, or a standalone paper in the monograph \\\"Constantine's Villa at Mediana\\\" itself? The Academia upload date (ID 44911502, ~2020-2021) doesn't match 2016 monograph... but Academia users often upload old papers late. Or it could be a chapter in a different volume.\\n\\nLet me look at the details around lines 44309-44340 for the \\\"Carska ideologija\\\" record, and 3080-3130 for the Archaeologia Bulgarica paper (bitstream available?), and 43840-43878 for record 1538.\",\"signature\":\"2c449052ead74aaaa110c515\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":0}},\"attributionAgent\":\"general-purpose\",\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"55ee88a3-3225-4247-b0e7-6357ce1a79ca\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-25T22:07:32.793Z\",\"effort\":\"high\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"sdk-cli\",\"cwd\":\"C:\\\\Svemir\\\\data\\\\sessions\\\\c1792946760393lb6a\\\\medijana_baza\\\\roj_glm\\\\objekti_CD\",\"sessionId\":\"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d\",\"version\":\"2.1.232\",\"gitBranch\":\"master\",\"slug\":\"cached-soaring-sedgewick\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"55ee88a3-3225-4247-b0e7-6357ce1a79ca\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a7308cdff85b75b5c\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"msg_20261026060723332ef5ee2cb345d0\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Tri rada Gordane Milošević u RAI. Gledam pune zapise — identifikatore, godine, bitestream PDF-ove.\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":0}},\"attributionAgent\":\"general-purpose\",\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"c2117f51-3e8b-4ff0-9634-4d70f48b76f0\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-25T22:07:33.885Z\",\"effort\":\"high\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"sdk-cli\",\"cwd\":\"C:\\\\Svemir\\\\data\\\\sessions\\\\c1792946760393lb6a\\\\medijana_baza\\\\roj_glm\\\\objekti_CD\",\"sessionId\":\"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d\",\"version\":\"2.1.232\",\"gitBranch\":\"master\",\"slug\":\"cached-soaring-sedgewick\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"c2117f51-3e8b-4ff0-9634-4d70f48b76f0\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a7308cdff85b75b5c\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"msg_20261026060723332ef5ee2cb345d0\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_d27d14e06f234650b2219507\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"C:\\\\Svemir\\\\data\\\\sessions\\\\c1792946760393lb6a\\\\medijana_baza\\\\roj_glm\\\\objekti_CD\\\\oai_full.xml\",\"limit\":45,\"offset\":3092}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":0}},\"attributionAgent\":\"general-purpose\",\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"b6e4b39f-79dc-40b2-a10e-76adfbddb740\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-25T22:07:33.888Z\",\"effort\":\"high\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"sdk-cli\",\"cwd\":\"C:\\\\Svemir\\\\data\\\\sessions\\\\c1792946760393lb6a\\\\medijana_baza\\\\roj_glm\\\\objekti_CD\",\"sessionId\":\"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d\",\"version\":\"2.1.232\",\"gitBranch\":\"master\",\"slug\":\"cached-soaring-sedgewick\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"b6e4b39f-79dc-40b2-a10e-76adfbddb740\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"promptId\":\"8f7a7d2d-dfff-49d8-9afd-b83bde684221\",\"agentId\":\"a7308cdff85b75b5c\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"call_d27d14e06f234650b2219507\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"3092\\t<dc:title>Excavations of Mediana in 2010 and 2011</dc:title>\\n3093\\t<dc:creator>Vasić, Miloje</dc:creator>\\n3094\\t<dc:creator>Milošević, Gordana</dc:creator>\\n3095\\t<dc:creator>Gavrilović, Nadežda</dc:creator>\\n3096\\t<dc:subject>Medijana</dc:subject>\\n3097\\t<dc:subject>vila s peristilom</dc:subject>\\n3098\\t<dc:subject>stratigrafija</dc:subject>\\n3099\\t<dc:subject>arhitektura</dc:subject>\\n3100\\t<dc:subject>pokretni nalazi</dc:subject>\\n3101\\t<dc:subject>kasna antika</dc:subject>\\n3102\\t<dc:description>Throughout 2010 and 2011, a systematic nine month archaeological exploration\\n3103\\t   was conducted on the north-eastern, northwestern and south-eastern parts of\\n3104\\t   the villa with peristyle, as well as the area in front of the museum building\\n3105\\t   (see note 8). The envisaged area of exploration was around 1,400 m². In\\n3106\\t   total, 1,230 m² of this area was thoroughly examined (Fig. 1). The\\n3107\\t   excavations were performed with the aim of defining the dimensions of the\\n3108\\t   north-western and south-western parts of the villa, the appearance of the\\n3109\\t   villa’s entrance, as well as to explore the foundations of the museum\\n3110\\t   building. In the course of the excavations, certain differences were\\n3111\\t   perceived in the stratigraphy of the villa with peristyle and the part\\n3112\\t   excavated outside the villa.</dc:description>\\n3113\\t<dc:date>2022-05-10T11:23:58Z</dc:date>\\n3114\\t<dc:date>2022-05-10T11:23:58Z</dc:date>\\n3115\\t<dc:date>2014</dc:date>\\n3116\\t<dc:type>article</dc:type>\\n3117\\t<dc:type>publishedVersion</dc:type>\\n3118\\t<dc:identifier>0350-0241</dc:identifier>\\n3119\\t<dc:identifier>https://rai.ai.ac.rs/handle/123456789/210</dc:identifier>\\n3120\\t<dc:identifier>10.2298/STA1464231V</dc:identifier>\\n3121\\t<dc:identifier>http://rai.ai.ac.rs/bitstream/id/92/207.pdf</dc:identifier>\\n3122\\t<dc:rights>openAccess</dc:rights>\\n3123\\t<dc:rights>https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/</dc:rights>\\n3124\\t<dc:rights>BY-NC-ND</dc:rights>\\n3125\\t<dc:publisher>Arheološki institut, Beograd</dc:publisher>\\n3126\\t<dc:source>Starinar</dc:source>\\n3127\\t</oai_dc:dc></metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:rai.ai.ac.rs:123456789/211</identifier><datestamp>2022-05-10T11:24:03Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_123456789_1</setSpec><setSpec>col_123456789_3</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc=\\\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/\\\" xmlns:doc=\\\"http://www.lyncode.com/xoai\\\" xmlns:xsi=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\\\" xmlns:dc=\\\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\\\" xsi:schemaLocation=\\\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd\\\">\\n3128\\t<dc:title>Corded Ware in the Central and Southern Balkans: A Consequence of Cultural Interaction or an Indication of Ethnic Change?</dc:title>\\n3129\\t<dc:creator>Bulatović, Aleksandar</dc:creator>\\n3130\\t<dc:description>The analysis of corded ware and accompanying artifacts reveals the nature of its appearance across the Central and Southern Balkan Eneolithic during three cultural-chronological horizons. The first horizon corresponds to the Early Eneolithic, namely the Bubanj-Salcuta-Krivodol cultural complex (BSK), while the second corresponds to the Cotofeni culture. The third horizon, showing chronological continuity with the second, and set within the Late Eneolithic/ Early Bronze Age, has a site distribution that encompasses the territory of nearly the entire Balkan Peninsula, where corded ware is found together with other steppe elements which are present in large numbers, such are burials under mounds and the appearance of the domestic horse.</dc:description>\\n3131\\t<dc:date>2022-05-10T11:24:03Z</dc:date>\\n3132\\t<dc:date>2022-05-10T11:24:03Z</dc:date>\\n3133\\t<dc:date>2014</dc:date>\\n3134\\t<dc:type>article</dc:type>\\n3135\\t<dc:type>publishedVersion</dc:type>\\n3136\\t<dc:identifier>0092-2323</dc:identifier>\"}]},\"uuid\":\"1fa8ef64-393e-436b-8ed6-fc737314a695\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-25T22:07:33.907Z\",\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"b6e4b39f-79dc-40b2-a10e-76adfbddb740\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"sdk-cli\",\"cwd\":\"C:\\\\Svemir\\\\data\\\\sessions\\\\c1792946760393lb6a\\\\medijana_baza\\\\roj_glm\\\\objekti_CD\",\"sessionId\":\"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d\",\"version\":\"2.1.232\",\"gitBranch\":\"master\",\"slug\":\"cached-soaring-sedgewick\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"1fa8ef64-393e-436b-8ed6-fc737314a695\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a7308cdff85b75b5c\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"msg_20261026060723332ef5ee2cb345d0\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_9e43d04d2b144de2a7cfd04b\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"C:\\\\Svemir\\\\data\\\\sessions\\\\c1792946760393lb6a\\\\medijana_baza\\\\roj_glm\\\\objekti_CD\\\\oai_full.xml\",\"limit\":35,\"offset\":44314}}],\"stop_reason\":\"tool_use\",\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":1244,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":46976,\"output_tokens\":673,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"thinking_tokens\":0},\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"stop_details\":null},\"attributionAgent\":\"general-purpose\",\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"4a361411-960a-4e86-b9c5-5dbcaac6a9ca\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-25T22:07:34.542Z\",\"effort\":\"high\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"sdk-cli\",\"cwd\":\"C:\\\\Svemir\\\\data\\\\sessions\\\\c1792946760393lb6a\\\\medijana_baza\\\\roj_glm\\\\objekti_CD\",\"sessionId\":\"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d\",\"version\":\"2.1.232\",\"gitBranch\":\"master\",\"slug\":\"cached-soaring-sedgewick\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"4a361411-960a-4e86-b9c5-5dbcaac6a9ca\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a7308cdff85b75b5c\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"msg_20261026060723332ef5ee2cb345d0\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_d64a66f5f54e4023a4ea5248\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"C:\\\\Svemir\\\\data\\\\sessions\\\\c1792946760393lb6a\\\\medijana_baza\\\\roj_glm\\\\objekti_CD\\\\oai_full.xml\",\"limit\":40,\"offset\":43840}}],\"stop_reason\":\"tool_use\",\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":1244,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":46976,\"output_tokens\":673,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"thinking_tokens\":0},\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"stop_details\":null},\"attributionAgent\":\"general-purpose\",\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"0b12afc6-6da7-402a-8434-943569b9560c\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-25T22:07:34.547Z\",\"effort\":\"high\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"sdk-cli\",\"cwd\":\"C:\\\\Svemir\\\\data\\\\sessions\\\\c1792946760393lb6a\\\\medijana_baza\\\\roj_glm\\\\objekti_CD\",\"sessionId\":\"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d\",\"version\":\"2.1.232\",\"gitBranch\":\"master\",\"slug\":\"cached-soaring-sedgewick\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"4a361411-960a-4e86-b9c5-5dbcaac6a9ca\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"promptId\":\"8f7a7d2d-dfff-49d8-9afd-b83bde684221\",\"agentId\":\"a7308cdff85b75b5c\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"call_9e43d04d2b144de2a7cfd04b\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"44314\\t<dc:title>Carska ideologija u arhitekturi, umetnosti i skulpturi rimske vile na Medijani</dc:title>\\n44315\\t<dc:creator>Milošević, Gordana</dc:creator>\\n44316\\t<dc:creator>Gavrilović, Nadežda</dc:creator>\\n44317\\t<dc:subject>Konstantin Veliki</dc:subject>\\n44318\\t<dc:subject>Naissus</dc:subject>\\n44319\\t<dc:subject>carska ideologija</dc:subject>\\n44320\\t<dc:subject>Medijana</dc:subject>\\n44321\\t<dc:description>U radu se raspravlja o novim tumacenjima rimske vile na suburbiumu Medijana. Na prostoru Medijane konstatovano i sistematski istraženo više gradevina razlicitih funkcija, kao što su na vila sa peristilom i termama, vila sa oktogonom, skladišta sa radionicama i vojnim barakama, dve ranohrišcanske bazilike, nekropole i više manjih vseoskih vila. Nova arheološka istraživanja vile sa peristilom sprovedenim u periodu od 2010 do 2012. godine omogucila su potpuno sagledavanje i izdvajanje graditeljskih faza, kao i analizu celokupne umetnosti kasnoantickog perioda zastupljenu u fresko-slikarstvu, mozaicima, arhitektonskoj plastici i skulpturi. Jasno je utvrdeno da se promene na vili sa peristilom u reprezentativni rezidencijalni objekat mogu vezati za period i graditeljske poduhvate Konstantina Velikog u Nišu.</dc:description>\\n44322\\t<dc:date>2024-02-01T11:44:44Z</dc:date>\\n44323\\t<dc:date>2024-02-01T11:44:44Z</dc:date>\\n44324\\t<dc:date>2013</dc:date>\\n44325\\t<dc:type>bookPart</dc:type>\\n44326\\t<dc:type>publishedVersion</dc:type>\\n44327\\t<dc:identifier>978-86-7148-176-2</dc:identifier>\\n44328\\t<dc:identifier>https://rai.ai.ac.rs/handle/123456789/1555</dc:identifier>\\n44329\\t<dc:identifier>http://rai.ai.ac.rs/bitstream/id/4442/bitstream_4442.pdf</dc:identifier>\\n44330\\t<dc:identifier>https://hdl.handle.net/21.15107/rcub_rai_1555</dc:identifier>\\n44331\\t<dc:language>sr</dc:language>\\n44332\\t<dc:relation>info:eu-repo/grantAgreement/MESTD/Basic Research (BR or ON)/177007/RS//</dc:relation>\\n44333\\t<dc:rights>openAccess</dc:rights>\\n44334\\t<dc:rights>ARR</dc:rights>\\n44335\\t<dc:publisher>Niš : Pravni fakultet Univerziteta u Nišu</dc:publisher>\\n44336\\t<dc:source>Zbornik radova 1700 godina Milanskog edikta</dc:source>\\n44337\\t</oai_dc:dc></metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:rai.ai.ac.rs:123456789/1563</identifier><datestamp>2026-05-07T10:24:07Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_123456789_1</setSpec><setSpec>col_123456789_3</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc=\\\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/\\\" xmlns:doc=\\\"http://www.lyncode.com/xoai\\\" xmlns:xsi=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\\\" xmlns:dc=\\\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\\\" xsi:schemaLocation=\\\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd\\\">\\n44338\\t<dc:title>Thracian Influence in Asia Minor Mystery Cults in the Eastern Parts of the Roman Provinces in the Central Balkans</dc:title>\\n44339\\t<dc:creator>Gavrilović Vitas, Nadežda</dc:creator>\\n44340\\t<dc:subject>Asia Minor cults</dc:subject>\\n44341\\t<dc:subject>Central Balkans</dc:subject>\\n44342\\t<dc:subject>mistery religions</dc:subject>\\n44343\\t<dc:subject>funerary rites</dc:subject>\\n44344\\t<dc:subject>snake</dc:subject>\\n44345\\t<dc:description>During the period of Roman rule in the Central Balkan Roman provinces,&#xd;\\n44346\\tamong other oriental cults, like the Syrian cult of Sol Invictus or the Persian cult of&#xd;\\n44347\\tMithras, Asia Minor deities and theologies were considerably favoured. Epigraphic and archaeological evidence confirms the existence of the cults of Magna Mater, Attis, Iuppiter Dolichenus, Sabazius, Iuppiter Turmasgades, Iuppiter Melanus, Men and Artemis of Ephesus. However, in the eastern parts of the Central Balkan Roman provinces, certain religious syncretism is emphasized, which can be connected to the strong Thracian influence in the mentioned territory. This paper examines the ways and the degree to which Thracian culture penetrated the religious beliefs and funerary rites of the population that inhabited the eastern parts of the Central Balkans in Antiquity.</dc:description>\\n44348\\t<dc:description>Bulletin of the national archaeological Institute XLIV</dc:description>\"}]},\"uuid\":\"2662a677-bfcf-4efd-a123-e1e3dc7a7a28\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-25T22:07:34.563Z\",\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"4a361411-960a-4e86-b9c5-5dbcaac6a9ca\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"sdk-cli\",\"cwd\":\"C:\\\\Svemir\\\\data\\\\sessions\\\\c1792946760393lb6a\\\\medijana_baza\\\\roj_glm\\\\objekti_CD\",\"sessionId\":\"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d\",\"version\":\"2.1.232\",\"gitBranch\":\"master\",\"slug\":\"cached-soaring-sedgewick\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"0b12afc6-6da7-402a-8434-943569b9560c\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"promptId\":\"8f7a7d2d-dfff-49d8-9afd-b83bde684221\",\"agentId\":\"a7308cdff85b75b5c\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"call_d64a66f5f54e4023a4ea5248\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"43840\\t<dc:description>Tübinger Archäologische Forschungen, Bd. 31</dc:description>\\n43841\\t<dc:date>2024-01-31T09:48:43Z</dc:date>\\n43842\\t<dc:date>2024-01-31T09:48:43Z</dc:date>\\n43843\\t<dc:date>2021</dc:date>\\n43844\\t<dc:type>bookPart</dc:type>\\n43845\\t<dc:type>publishedVersion</dc:type>\\n43846\\t<dc:identifier>978-3-89646-862-8</dc:identifier>\\n43847\\t<dc:identifier>https://rai.ai.ac.rs/handle/123456789/1537</dc:identifier>\\n43848\\t<dc:identifier>https://hdl.handle.net/21.15107/rcub_rai_1537</dc:identifier>\\n43849\\t<dc:language>en</dc:language>\\n43850\\t<dc:rights>restrictedAccess</dc:rights>\\n43851\\t<dc:rights>ARR</dc:rights>\\n43852\\t<dc:publisher>Rahden/Westf.: Leidorf</dc:publisher>\\n43853\\t<dc:source>People Abroad. Proceedings of the XVI International Colloquium on Roman Provincial Art</dc:source>\\n43854\\t</oai_dc:dc></metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:rai.ai.ac.rs:123456789/1538</identifier><datestamp>2025-01-13T10:04:04Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_123456789_1</setSpec><setSpec>col_123456789_3</setSpec><setSpec>col_123456789_413</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc=\\\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/\\\" xmlns:doc=\\\"http://www.lyncode.com/xoai\\\" xmlns:xsi=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\\\" xmlns:dc=\\\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\\\" xsi:schemaLocation=\\\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd\\\">\\n43855\\t<dc:title>Kult Herkula i Merkura u Gornjoj Meziji I-IV vek n. e.</dc:title>\\n43856\\t<dc:title>The Cults of Hercules and Mercury in Upper Moesia from the first to the fourth century</dc:title>\\n43857\\t<dc:creator>Gavrilović, Nadežda</dc:creator>\\n43858\\t<dc:subject>Rimski kultovi</dc:subject>\\n43859\\t<dc:subject>provincijalna religija</dc:subject>\\n43860\\t<dc:subject>Herkul</dc:subject>\\n43861\\t<dc:subject>Merkur</dc:subject>\\n43862\\t<dc:description>Monografija \\\"Kult Herkula i Merkura u Gornjoj Meziji od I-IV veka n. e.\\\" predstavlja studiju o do sada poznatim, dokumentovanim, analiziranim i interpretiranim epigrafskim i arheološkim spomenicima u vezi sa kultovima rimskih bogova Herkula i Merkura sa teritorije rimske provincije Gornje Mezije.</dc:description>\\n43863\\t<dc:description>Posebna izdanja, vol. 56.</dc:description>\\n43864\\t<dc:date>2024-01-31T09:51:51Z</dc:date>\\n43865\\t<dc:date>2024-01-31T09:51:51Z</dc:date>\\n43866\\t<dc:date>2014</dc:date>\\n43867\\t<dc:type>book</dc:type>\\n43868\\t<dc:type>publishedVersion</dc:type>\\n43869\\t<dc:identifier>978-86-80093-92-5</dc:identifier>\\n43870\\t<dc:identifier>https://rai.ai.ac.rs/handle/123456789/1538</dc:identifier>\\n43871\\t<dc:i