mić 2017 (Ante Portam Auream, studia in honorem Aleksandar Jovanović) contains:\\n\\n1. **Milošević 2013** — \\\"G. Milošević, Arhitektura rezidencijalnog kompleksa na Medijani, u: Konstantin Veliki i Milanski edikt 313. Rađanje hrišćanstva u rimskim provincijama na tlu Srbije, I. Popović, B. Borić-Bresković (ur.), Beograd 2013, 118-125.\\\" — This is the Serbian-language counterpart! \\\"Arhitektura rezidencijalnog kompleksa na Medijani\\\" = \\\"Architecture of the residential complex at Mediana\\\". Hmm — not exactly \\\"Urbanism and Architecture of the Imperial Domain at Mediana\\\" but related.\\n\\n2. **Milošević, Peters, Wendling 2011** — \\\"G. Milošević, D. Peters, H. Wendling, Geophysical survey at late Roman Mediana, [Starinar] LXI 2011, 275-284.\\\" — the geophysics paper (the base already knows Starinar 61/2011 — 16 structures!).\\n\\n3. Vasić 2005 — \\\"Mediana - domaine impérial ou bien privé?\\\", in Römische Städte und Festungen an der Donau, Beograd 2005, 167-176.\\n4. Vasić 2006 — Stibadium in Romuliana and Mediana.\\n5. Vasić 2007 — \\\"Mediana — eine kaiserliche Villa bei Niš\\\", in: U. Brandl, M. Vasić, Roms Erbe auf dem Balkan. Spätantike Kaiservillen und Stadtanlagen in Serbien, Mainz am Rhein 2007, 96-197. — a major German monograph chapter.\\n6. M. R. Vasić 2013 — Gradovi i carske vile..., 76-101.\\n7. Petrović 1994 — Medijana. Rezidencija rimskih careva, Beograd 1994.\\n8. Zotović, Petrović 1969 — known.\\n\\nSo — the Academia paper \\\"Urbanism and Architecture of the Imperial Domain at Mediana\\\" — where from? Now with \\\"Arhitektura rezidencijalnog kompleksa na Medijani\\\" (2013, Beograd, Konstantin Veliki i Milanski edikt 313) known... The Academia title is different. Possibly:\\n- It's the English original/version of the 2013 Serbian paper, unpublished manuscript uploaded to Academia.\\n- Or a chapter in \\\"Roms Erbe auf dem Balkan\\\" (2007)? No — that's Vasić's.\\n- Or a paper in a volume like \\\"Roman Imperial Estates\\\"/\\\"Palace economies\\\"?\\n\\nHmm. Actually — wait. Let me think about \\\"The Imperial Domain at Mediana\\\" phrasing. There is a known English-language volume: \\\"Mediana. The Imperial Domain\\\" or maybe the paper appeared in the volume of the 22nd Limes Congress? Or in \\\"The Roman Imperial Estates\\\" theme?\\n\\nActually, I recall the RAI OAI has items with English titles about Mediana — let me systematically list ALL Mediana-related records in oai_full.xml with their creators, to see if there's a paper by Milošević with an English title I haven't seen. Earlier grep showed titles but I filtered only some. Let me list all dc:title lines containing Mediana/Medijana plus their following creator lines. Actually easier: grep -o \\\"dc:title>[^<]*Mediana[^<]*\\\" then check creators nearby. We already saw the main ones.\\n\\nAlternative: the Academia paper might be published in the volume \\\"Niš i Vizantija\\\" or in the \\\"Constantine's Villa at Mediana\\\" monograph (2016). The monograph \\\"Constantine's Villa at Mediana\\\" (National Museum Niš 2016) — a bilingual/English catalog-monograph — could contain Milošević's chapter \\\"Urbanism and Architecture of the Imperial Domain at Mediana\\\". That remains the top hypothesis; the Academia upload would then be the author's self-archived chapter.\\n\\nLet me now try to verify via the RAI handle page or PDF. webReader is still 429... Let me try again — it's been several minutes of local greps. If it fails, try rai.ai.ac.rs server API? The DSpace 5.10 (RAI runs DSpace 5.10 per rai_api_mediana.html) — REST API at /rest/handle/... Actually rai_test.html might be a saved DSpace REST test. Let me check rai_test.html and rai_search2.html quickly for anything useful.\",\"signature\":\"c4768dd6a085425b8a819360\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":0}},\"attributionAgent\":\"general-purpose\",\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"674f3897-a440-4747-abe5-329aeb98c460\",\