,\"stop_details\":null},\"attributionAgent\":\"general-purpose\",\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"d63fd0e4-0a43-4659-9d5c-66e93de2ff9d\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-25T22:10:22.147Z\",\"effort\":\"high\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"sdk-cli\",\"cwd\":\"C:\\\\Svemir\\\\data\\\\sessions\\\\c1792946760393lb6a\\\\medijana_baza\\\\roj_glm\\\\objekti_CD\",\"sessionId\":\"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d\",\"version\":\"2.1.232\",\"gitBranch\":\"master\",\"slug\":\"cached-soaring-sedgewick\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"d63fd0e4-0a43-4659-9d5c-66e93de2ff9d\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"af3648b6823f6e54f\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"msg_20261026060957d4ef7351efc64d51\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_e72b5790d1d746dcb1407f60\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"C:/Svemir/data/sessions/c1792946760393lb6a/medijana_baza/roj_glm/objekti_CD/skinuto/tapavicki_2011.txt\"}}],\"stop_reason\":\"tool_use\",\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":3123,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":114496,\"output_tokens\":1522,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"thinking_tokens\":0},\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"stop_details\":null},\"attributionAgent\":\"general-purpose\",\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"a63c663c-f441-45df-b33d-ba2ce005f4d9\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-25T22:10:22.222Z\",\"effort\":\"high\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"sdk-cli\",\"cwd\":\"C:\\\\Svemir\\\\data\\\\sessions\\\\c1792946760393lb6a\\\\medijana_baza\\\\roj_glm\\\\objekti_CD\",\"sessionId\":\"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d\",\"version\":\"2.1.232\",\"gitBranch\":\"master\",\"slug\":\"cached-soaring-sedgewick\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"a63c663c-f441-45df-b33d-ba2ce005f4d9\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"promptId\":\"8f7a7d2d-dfff-49d8-9afd-b83bde684221\",\"agentId\":\"af3648b6823f6e54f\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"call_e72b5790d1d746dcb1407f60\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\t                                                  MEDIANA 2011\\n2\\t\\n3\\t         The archaeological site Mediana covers the area of 80 ha and it is situated in the non-urban\\n4\\tNis zone. The excavation in 2011 brought research of the villa with peristyle to an end. It is a\\n5\\tlongitudinal structure that runs NE � SW and covers the area of about 6500 m2. It possesses a\\n6\\tcentral part in the shape of a peristyle and a monumental audience hall in the north, but also a large\\n7\\tnumber of rooms of administrative and residential character on both sides of the peristyle.\\n8\\t\\n9\\t         The 2011 excavation was aimed at the northern, residential villa part, rooms around the\\n10\\ttriclinium and the rooms in the south, i.e., at the villa entrance. Two trenches were opened in the\\n11\\tNE villa corner marked as 95 (7.30  2 m) and 96 (3.80  2 m). Two control trenches in the room\\n12\\tmarked -22 contained layers of ancient rubble, lying of an older mortar floor. Beneath it there was\\n13\\ta hypocaust.\\n14\\t\\n15\\t         In this area, running north, trench 97 was opened and to the north from it trenches 98, 103\\n16\\tand 104. In trench 97 (6.70  4 m), a rectangular structure made of boulders in a dry wall was\\n17\\tunearthed, leaning on the northern villa facade.\\n18\\t\\n19\\t         In the control profile between the trenches 46 and 47 a marble head of a goddess was\\n20\\tdiscovered, most likely Venus or Diana. In the western room 22, the existence of two mortar floors\\n21\\twas confirmed. On the northern fa�ade and within trench 72 remains of a destroyed furnace\\n22\\t(_praefurnium_) were discovered (Fig. 1), indicating that during the second villa phase, the\\n23\\tpraefurnium and the hypocaust were no longer in use.\\n24\\t\\n25\\t         Walls of the room 22 were decorated with frescos. On the floor of this room, a large\\n26\\tconcentration of wattle with reed imprints was unearthed, originating from the ceiling and bearing\\n27\\ttraces of frescos, which meant that the ceiling was painted, too.\\n28\\t\\n29\\t         Trenches outside the NW villa corner include stibadium B and the area around it. The\\n30\\tentrance into stibadium B was positioned in the south. On the northern side, beneath the stibadium,\\n31\\ta destroyed hypocaust furnace was discovered. On the eastern and the western stibadium side,\\n32\\trectangular annexes were unearthed with mosaic decorated floors and walls plated with marble. It is\\n33\\tcertain that stibadium B was later added to the northern fa�ade, while stibadium A was erected\\n34\\tsimultaneously with the villa itself. During this campaign, the mosaic with floral ad geometrical\\n35\\tmotifs was fully unearthed. A large number of mosaic tiles (_tesserae_) made of glass was found,\\n36\\tindicating that the ceiling was also decorated with mosaic.\\n37\\t\\n38\\t         This year's excavations confirmed that during the second building horizon (from about 330\\n39\\tto 378) there were two building phases. During the second phase, the villa was decorated with\\n40\\tmosaics, frescos and sculptures. Although during the first phase, the structure mainly played an\\n41\\tadministrative role, during the second one, it became a luxurious residence with ceremonial\\n42\\tcharacter.\\n43\\t\\n44\\tSource: Gavrilovi N., Arheoloska istrazivanja na Medijani u 2011. godini, Arheologija u Srbiji\\n45\\t(Projekti Arheoloskog instituta u 2011. godini), Beograd 2012, 78-81.\\n46\\t\\fFig. 1. ediana, northern profile of the room 22 and hypocaust remains with praefurnium (after:\\n47\\tGavrilovi 2012, 78, Sl. 2).\\n48\\t\\n49\\tFig. 2. diana, mosaic with geometrical and floral motifs in stibadium B (after: Gavrilovi 2012,\\n50\\t79, Sl. 1).\\n51\\t\\n52\\tFig. 3. diana, the southern porch of the villa with peristyle (after: Gavrilovi 2012, 80, Sl. 3).\\n53\\t\\n54\\tBibliography:\\n55\\t\\n56\\t .,  �   , , 1994.\\n57\\t\\n58\\tVasi M., Bronze Railing from Mediana,  LIII�LIV/ 2003�2004, 79-109, Beograd.\\n59\\t\\n60\\t                                                 ME 2011\\n61\\t\\n62\\t                80    \\n63\\t.   2011.        .\\n64\\t     ,    -, \\n65\\t  6500 2.           \\n66\\t  ,      - \\n67\\t   .\\n68\\t\\n69\\t          2011.      ,  \\n70\\t,          .   \\n71\\t          95 (7,30  2 )  96 (3,80  2\\n72\\t).      -22     ,  \\n73\\t    .     .\\n74\\t\\n75\\t           ,   ,     97,      98,\\n76\\t103  104.   97 (6,70  4 )       \\n77\\t,     .\\n78\\t\\n79\\t              46  47     ,\\n80\\t   .    22,    \\n81\\t .       72    \\n82\\t (. 1),           \\n83\\t .\\n84\\t\\n85\\t           22    .     \\n86\\t              \\n87\\t,         .\\n88\\t\\n89\\t                    .\\n90\\t       .   ,  ,  \\n91\\t  .        \\n92\\t           \\n93\\t.           ,   \\n94\\t\\f         .      \\n95\\t      .      \\n96\\t ,           .\\n97\\t\\n98\\t                  \\n99\\t(  330.  378)    .   ,    \\n100\\t,   .         \\n101\\t ,       \\n102\\t.\\n103\\t\\n104\\t: Gavrilovi N., Arheoloska istrazivanja na Medijani u 2011. godini, Arheologija u Srbiji\\n105\\t(Projekti Arheoloskog instituta u 2011. godini), Beograd 2012, 78-81.\\n106\\t\\n107\\t. 1. ,    22     \\n108\\t(: Gavrilovi 2012, 78, Sl. 2).\\n109\\t. 2. ,          (:\\n110\\tGavrilovi 2012, 79, Sl. 1).\\n111\\t. 3. ,      (: Gavrilovi 2012, 80, Sl. 3).\\n112\\t\\n113\\t:\\n114\\t 1994 � . ,  �   , .\\n115\\tVasi 2004 � M. Vasi, Bronze Railing from Mediana,  LIII�LIV/ 2003�2004, Beograd\\n116\\t\\f\\f\\f\"}]},\"uuid\":\"e9ab1748-f48d-4981-a47d-5a78a4fbf754\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-25T22:10:22.231Z\",\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"a63c663c-f441-45df-b33d-ba2ce005f4d9\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"sdk-cli\",\"cwd\":\"C:\\\\Svemir\\\\data\\\\sessions\\\\c1792946760393lb6a\\\\medijana_baza\\\\roj_glm\\\\objekti_CD\",\"sessionId\":\"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d\",\"version\":\"2.1.232\",\"gitBranch\":\"master\",\"slug\":\"cached-soaring-sedgewick\"}\n</output>"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d","uuid":"7d7eee40-25b3-4360-a278-2d3f8cce0f72","timestamp":"2026-10-25T22:10:22.377Z","tool_use_result":{"retrieval_status":"not_ready","task":{"task_id":"af3648b6823f6e54f","task_type":"local_agent","status":"running","description":"Lov na Jeremić 2006 mozaici","prompt":"Sesija ti je prekinuta; transkript ti je sačuvan. Nastavi gde si stao i predaj konačan izveštaj. Dopuna stanja iz glavne niti: nađen je Gordana Jeremić (Institute of Archaeology Belgrade) — \"New Archaeological Data on the Mosaics in Mediana near Nis\" (2009, apstrakt skinut lokalno: novac Konstancija II 341–346 ispod mozaika severnog trema peristila = terminus post quem). Traži dalje: (1) pun tekst toga rada (simpozijum? zbornik?), (2) Jeremić 2006 o mozaicima Medijane (Niš i Vizantija 4?), (3) Jeremić, \"Meduza\"/medaljon aule (2017, PDF već skinut u glavnoj niti — ne troši vreme na to), (4) radovi o objektima A/B/C/D Medijane. Vrati izveštaj: naslov, autor, godina, izdanje, strane, URL, šta donosi, poverenje; šta ostaje zatvoreno.","result":"{\"parentUuid\":null,\"isSidechain\":true,\"promptId\":\"bdca32e7-5725-4bf7-b673-b573632769f3\",\"agentId\":\"af3648b6823f6e54f\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Istraživački zadatak (arheologija, rimski mozaici, Medijana/Naissus, Niš, Srbija). Tražiš:\\n\\n1. Jeremić G. 2006 — monografski/opširni rad o mozaicima Medijane. Baza zna samo da je to verovatno \\\"Niš i Vizantija 4\\\" (zbornik Centra za crkvene studije, Niš). Pronađi tačan naslov rada, strane, i idealno pun tekst (zbornici \\\"Niš i Vizantija\\\" ponegde su besplatno na internetu — potraži na sccs.rs, crkvene studije, ili PDF zbornika Niš i Vizantija 4 (2006?); takođe academia.edu (iza prijave — zapiši kao ograničenje), scribd, archive.org).\\n2. SVE radove autora/ke G. Jeremić (verovatno Gordana Jeremić, arheolog/kinja Narodnog muzeja Niš) o Medijani — naročito ako obrađuju \\\"objekat A\\\", \\\"objekat B\\\", \\\"objekat C\\\", \\\"objekat D\\\" kompleksa Medijana (objekti van vile sa peristilom, označeni slovima u literaturi Narodnog muzeja Niš).\\n\\nPretraga na srpskom i engleskom: \\\"Jeremić\\\" \\\"Medijana\\\" mozaici; \\\"Gordana Jeremić\\\" Mediana; \\\"Niš i Vizantija 4\\\" PDF; site:doiserbia.nb.rs Jeremić Mediana; site:scindeks.nc.rs medijana mozaici; Google Scholar. Koristi WebSearch i WebFetch/mcp__web_reader__webReader. SCIndeks (scindeks.nc.rs) često ima apstrakte besplatno — to je koristan nivo poverenja \\\"srednje\\\".\\n\\nPAŽNJA — ZAMKA: mere \\\"objekat A 17,20×14,60 m / objekat B 20,30×14,18 / objekat C delimično\\\" su iz Mlinčića-Tisine kod Zenice, NE sa Medijane — ne primaj kao podatak o Medijani.\\n\\nNE piši nikakve fajlove. Vrati izveštaj kao čist tekst (srpski, latinica): za svaki pogodak — naslov, autor, godina, izvor/zbornik, strane, tačan URL, šta donosi (mere mozaika, tehniku, položaje, podatke o objektima A–D), nivo poverenja (visoko = pun tekst; srednje = apstrakt/fragment/citat; nisko = samo bibliografija). Na kraju iskreno šta ostaje zatvoreno.\"},\"uuid\":\"85d5791b-6179-48e4-9c88-a65bdb5beb2e\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-25T21:43:38.658Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"sdk-cli\",\"cwd\":\"C:\\\\Svemir\\\\data\\\\sessions\\\\c1792946760393lb6a\\\\medijana_baza\\\\roj_glm\\\\objekti_CD\",\"sessionId\":\"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d\",\"version\":\"2.1.232\",\"gitBranch\":\"master\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"85d5791b-6179-48e4-9c88-a65bdb5beb2e\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"af3648b6823f6e54f\",\"attachment\":{\"type\":\"skill_listing\",\"content\":\"- dataviz: Use this skill whenever you are about to create ANY chart, graph, plot, dashboard, or data visualization, in ANY output medium — an HTML or React artifact, inline SVG, plotting code in any library (matplotlib, plotly, d3, Recharts, …), an image/PNG you will render and upload, or a chart shared into Slack. Read it BEFORE writing the first line of chart code, choosing chart colors, building a stat tile / meter / KPI row, or laying out a dashboard. Produces visualizations that read as one system — elegant, accessible, consistent in light and dark — using a brand-neutral placeholder palette you swap for your own. Teaches a design-system-agnostic method: a form heuristic, a color formula with a runnable validator, mark specs, and interaction rules. A validated default palette is documented in `references/palette.md` — swap that file's values for your brand's. Triggers on: \\\"chart\\\", \\\"graph\\\", \\\"plot\\\", \\\"data viz\\\", \\\"visualization\\\", \\\"dashboard\\\", \\\"analytics\\\", \\\"visualize data\\\", \\\"categorical colors\\\", \\\"sequential / diverging palette\\\", \\\"stat tile\\\", \\\"sparkline\\\", \\\"heatmap\\\", \\\"legend\\\", \\\"axis\\\", \\\"tooltip\\\", \\\"chart colors\\\", \\\"color by series\\\".\\n- update-config: Use this skill to configure the Claude Code harness via settings.json. Automated behaviors (\\\"from now on when X\\\", \\\"each time X\\\", \\\"whenever X\\\", \\\"before/after X\\\") require hooks configured in settings.json - the harness executes these, not Claude, so memory/preferences cannot fulfill them. Also use for: permissions (\\\"allow X\\\", \\\"add permission\\\", \\\"move permission to\\\"), env vars (\\\"set X=Y\\\"), hook troubleshooting, or any changes to settings.json/settings.local.json files. Examples: \\\"allow npm commands\\\", \\\"add bq permission to global settings\\\", \\\"move permission to user settings\\\", \\\"set DEBUG=true\\\", \\\"when claude stops show X\\\". For simple settings like theme/model, suggest the /config command.\\n- keybindings-help: Use when the user wants to customize keyboard shortcuts, rebind keys, add chord bindings, or modify ~/.claude/keybindings.json. Examples: \\\"rebind ctrl+s\\\", \\\"add a chord shortcut\\\", \\\"change the submit key\\\", \\\"customize keybindings\\\".\\n- simplify: Review the changed code for reuse, simplification, efficiency, and altitude cleanups, then apply the fixes. Quality only — it does not hunt for bugs; use /code-review for that.\\n- fewer-permission-prompts: Scan your transcripts for common read-only Bash and MCP tool calls, then add a prioritized allowlist to project .claude/settings.json to reduce permission prompts.\\n- loop: Run a prompt or slash command on a recurring interval (e.g. /loop 5m /foo, defaults to 10m) - When the user wants to set up a recurring task, poll for status, or run something repeatedly on an interval (e.g. \\\"check the deploy every 5 minutes\\\", \\\"keep running /babysit-prs\\\"). Do NOT invoke for one-off tasks.\\n- claude-api: Reference for the Claude API / Anthropic SDK — model ids, pricing, params, streaming, tool use, MCP, agents, caching, token counting, model migration.\\nTRIGGER — read BEFORE opening the target file; don't skip because it \\\"looks like a one-liner\\\" — whenever: the prompt names Claude/Anthropic in any form (Claude, Anthropic, Fable, Opus, Sonnet, Haiku, `anthropic`, `@anthropic-ai`, `claude-*`, `us.anthropic.*`, `[1m]`); the user asks about an LLM (pricing/model choice/limits/caching) — never answer from memory; OR the task is LLM-shaped with provider unstated (agent/MCP/tool-definition/multi-agent/RAG/LLM-judge/computer-use; generate/summarize/extract/classify/rewrite/converse over NL; debugging refusals/cutoffs/streaming/tool-calls/tokens).\\nSKIP only when another provider is being worked on (overrides all triggers): OpenAI/GPT/Gemini/Llama/Mistral/Cohere/Ollama named in the query; OR `grep -rE 'openai|langchain_openai|google.generativeai|genai|mistralai|cohere|ollama'` over the project hits (run this grep FIRST if no provider named — don't Read the file).\\n- run: Launch and drive this project's app to see a change working. Use when asked to run, start, or screenshot the app, or to confirm a change works in the real app (not just tests). First looks for a project skill that already covers launching the app; otherwise falls back to built-in patterns per project type (CLI, server, TUI, Electron, browser-driven, library).\\n- init: Initialize a new CLAUDE.md file with codebase documentation\\n- security-review: Complete a security review of the pending changes on the current branch\",\"skillCount\":10,\"isInitial\":true,\"names\":[\"dataviz\",\"update-config\",\"keybindings-help\",\"simplify\",\"fewer-permission-prompts\",\"loop\",\"claude-api\",\"run\",\"init\",\"security-review\"]},\"type\":\"attachment\",\"uuid\":\"27638e09-e069-4227-bea5-371d931f6855\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-25T21:43:38.661Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"sdk-cli\",\"cwd\":\"C:\\\\Svemir\\\\data\\\\sessions\\\\c1792946760393lb6a\\\\medijana_baza\\\\roj_glm\\\\objekti_CD\",\"sessionId\":\"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d\",\"version\":\"2.1.232\",\"gitBranch\":\"master\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"27638e09-e069-4227-bea5-371d931f6855\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"promptId\":\"8f7a7d2d-dfff-49d8-9afd-b83bde684221\",\"agentId\":\"af3648b6823f6e54f\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"The coordinator sent a message while you were working:\\nSesija ti je prekinuta; transkript ti je sačuvan. Nastavi gde si stao i predaj konačan izveštaj. Dopuna stanja iz glavne niti: nađen je Gordana Jeremić (Institute of Archaeology Belgrade) — \\\"New Archaeological Data on the Mosaics in Mediana near Nis\\\" (2009, apstrakt skinut lokalno: novac Konstancija II 341–346 ispod mozaika severnog trema peristila = terminus post quem). Traži dalje: (1) pun tekst toga rada (simpozijum? zbornik?), (2) Jeremić 2006 o mozaicima Medijane (Niš i Vizantija 4?), (3) Jeremić, \\\"Meduza\\\"/medaljon aule (2017, PDF već skinut u glavnoj niti — ne troši vreme na to), (4) radovi o objektima A/B/C/D Medijane. Vrati izveštaj: naslov, autor, godina, izdanje, strane, URL, šta donosi, poverenje; šta ostaje zatvoreno.\\n\\nAddress this before completing your current task.\"},\"isMeta\":true,\"uuid\":\"fa21727e-72ea-45ae-8280-651caf7cd595\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-25T22:04:09.078Z\",\"origin\":{\"kind\":\"coordinator\"},\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"sdk-cli\",\"cwd\":\"C:\\\\Svemir\\\\data\\\\sessions\\\\c1792946760393lb6a\\\\medijana_baza\\\\roj_glm\\\\objekti_CD\",\"sessionId\":\"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d\",\"version\":\"2.1.232\",\"gitBranch\":\"master\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"fa21727e-72ea-45ae-8280-651caf7cd595\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"af3648b6823f6e54f\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"msg_202610260604194f973aa79eee4f90\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"Let me understand the task. I'm a research agent investigating archaeological literature about Roman mosaics at Medijana (Mediana) near Niš, Serbia. I need to find:\\n\\n1. Jeremić G. 2006 — a monograph/extensive work on Medijana mosaics, possibly in \\\"Niš i Vizantija 4\\\" (a proceedings volume from Centar za crkvene studije, Niš). Find exact title, pages, ideally full text.\\n2. All works by G. Jeremić (likely Gordana Jeremić, archaeologist) about Medijana — especially if they cover \\\"objekat A\\\", \\\"objekat B\\\", \\\"objekat C\\\", \\\"objekat D\\\" of the Medijana complex.\\n\\nAdditional info from the coordinator:\\n- Found: Gordana Jeremić (Institute of Archaeology Belgrade) — \\\"New Archaeological Data on the Mosaics in Mediana near Nis\\\" (2009, abstract downloaded locally: coin of Constantius II 341–346 below the mosaic of the northern porch of the peristyle = terminus post quem).\\n- Looking for: (1) full text of that work (symposium? proceedings?), (2) Jeremić 2006 on Medijana mosaics (Niš i Vizantija 4?), (3) Jeremić \\\"Meduza\\\"/medallion of the aula (2017, PDF already downloaded in main thread — don't waste time), (4) works about objects A/B/C/D of Medijana.\\n\\nWatch out for the trap: measurements \\\"objekat A 17,20×14,60 m / objekat B 20,30×14,18 / objekat C partially\\\" are from Mlinčić-Tisine near Zenica (Bosnia), NOT Medijana.\\n\\nLet me first check what's already in the local working directory (maybe the abstract that was downloaded locally), then do web searches.\\n\\nLet me start by checking the local files to see what's already been gathered.\",\"signature\":\"2f075a4554f34b4f91de10a8\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":0}},\"attributionAgent\":\"general-purpose\",\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"5eb46fec-a2f7-4788-954c-e0e6ef82f5ec\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-25T22:04:26.977Z\",\"effort\":\"high\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"sdk-cli\",\"cwd\":\"C:\\\\Svemir\\\\data\\\\sessions\\\\c1792946760393lb6a\\\\medijana_baza\\\\roj_glm\\\\objekti_CD\",\"sessionId\":\"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d\",\"version\":\"2.1.232\",\"gitBranch\":\"master\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"5eb46fec-a2f7-4788-954c-e0e6ef82f5ec\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"af3648b6823f6e54f\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"msg_202610260604194f973aa79eee4f90\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_d617f9d128fc4a3d9c02b05a\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"ls -la \\\"C:/Svemir/data/sessions/c1792946760393lb6a/medijana_baza/roj_glm/objekti_CD\\\" 2>/dev/null; echo \\\"---\\\"; ls -la \\\"C:/Svemir/data/sessions/c1792946760393lb6a/medijana_baza/roj_glm\\\" 2>/dev/null | head -50\",\"description\":\"List working directory contents to see saved files\"}}],\"stop_reason\":\"tool_use\",\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2051,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read