lug\":\"cached-soaring-sedgewick\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"0611593e-9379-4269-8411-b23aa203f5ea\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"promptId\":\"8f7a7d2d-dfff-49d8-9afd-b83bde684221\",\"agentId\":\"af3648b6823f6e54f\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"call_1bd2ebbb83e64390a9bde3b4\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"27920\\t<dc:language>en</dc:language>\\n27921\\t<dc:relation>info:eu-repo/grantAgreement/MESTD/Basic Research (BR or ON)/177007/RS//</dc:relation>\\n27922\\t<dc:rights>openAccess</dc:rights>\\n27923\\t<dc:rights>https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/</dc:rights>\\n27924\\t<dc:rights>ARR</dc:rights>\\n27925\\t<dc:publisher>HERAedu</dc:publisher>\\n27926\\t<dc:source>Limes plus. Journal of Social Sciences and Humanities</dc:source>\\n27927\\t</oai_dc:dc></metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:rai.ai.ac.rs:123456789/938</identifier><datestamp>2023-11-27T11:13:54Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_123456789_1</setSpec><setSpec>col_123456789_3</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc=\\\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/\\\" xmlns:doc=\\\"http://www.lyncode.com/xoai\\\" xmlns:xsi=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\\\" xmlns:dc=\\\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\\\" xsi:schemaLocation=\\\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd\\\">\\n27928\\t<dc:title>Early Christian luxurious glass finds in Serbia</dc:title>\\n27929\\t<dc:creator>Jeremić, Gordana</dc:creator>\\n27930\\t<dc:subject>Luxurious glass / glass workshops / Late Antiquity / Early Christianity / Roman provinces / Serbia</dc:subject>\\n27931\\t<dc:description>The period of Late Antiquity was a prosperous age in the history of provinces that existed in the territory of the modern Republic of Serbia (Pannonia Secunda, Moesia Prima, Dacia Ripensis, Dacia Meditteraneaand Dardania). This prosperous period is embedded in the fact that several Roman emperors were born here who left significant influence in their birthplaces in construction activities including economy and other measures: Sirmium (Sremska Mitrovica) was one of the capitals in the Roman Empire, Romuliana (Gamzigrad), Šarkamen, and Naissus (Niš). The best way to track the Christianisation of the late antique cities in Serbia is with artefacts of the 4th and first half of the 5th centuries. During this period of prosperity luxurious glass vessels tell a story about the needs and tastes of the inhabitants in the Roman cities. The vessels were done in techniques of mosaic, fondi d`oro or with relief figural presentations or inscriptions. It was mostly discovered in the grave units or within settlement`s layers, as well as within the church buildings in the larger or small settlements: Sirmium, Kruševlje, Singidunum (Belgrade), Bor vicinity, Campsa (Ravna), Diana (Karataš), Aquae (Prahovo) and Mediana (Brzi Brod, Niš). Workshops for the manufacture of glass tableware from late antiquity have been discovered until present in Sirmium, Mediana near Naissus, as well as several sites close to the mine centres, however, it is possible that these supplied local and regional inhabitants. Luxurious vessels with Christian symbols or from a Christian context, especially those done by mosaic glass, could reach these areas by trade roads or as some present or moving.</dc:description>\\n27932\\t<dc:date>2023-11-23T11:34:22Z</dc:date>\\n27933\\t<dc:date>2023-11-23T11:34:22Z</dc:date>\\n27934\\t<dc:date>2018</dc:date>\\n27935\\t<dc:type>conferenceObject</dc:type>\\n27936\\t<dc:type>publishedVersion</dc:type>\\n27937\\t<dc:identifier>https://rai.ai.ac.rs/handle/123456789/938</dc:identifier>\\n27938\\t<dc:identifier>http://rai.ai.ac.rs/bitstream/id/2150/35_AIHV_2018_abstract.pdf</dc:identifier>\\n27939\\t<dc:identifier>https://hdl.handle.net/21.15107/rcub_rai_938</dc:identifier>\\n27940\\t<dc:language>en</dc:language>\\n27941\\t<dc:relation>info:eu-repo/grantAgreement/MESTD/Basic Research (BR or ON)/177007/RS//</dc:relation>\\n27942\\t<dc:rights>openAccess</dc:rights>\\n27943\\t<dc:rights>https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/</dc:rights>\\n27944\\t<dc:rights>ARR</dc:rights>\"}]},\"uuid\":\"fa188ce1-93ee-4c5e-b9fd-7dd45e249986\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-25T22:07:44.144Z\",\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"0611593e-9379-4269-8411-b23aa203f5ea\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"sdk-cli\",\"cwd\":\"C:\\\\Svemir\\\\data\\\\sessions\\\\c1792946760393lb6a\\\\medijana_baza\\\\roj_glm\\\\objekti_CD\",\"sessionId\":\"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d\",\"version\":\"2.1.232\",\"gitBranch\":\"master\",\"slug\":\"cached-soaring-sedgewick\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"fa188ce1-93ee-4c5e-b9fd-7dd45e249986\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"af3648b6823f6e54f\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"msg_2026102606073820d3cd4cada846e4\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_394132fe0ce147c0ac194367\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"C:/Svemir/data/sessions/c1792946760393lb6a/medijana_baza/roj_glm/objekti_CD/oai_full.xml\",\"limit\":25,\"offset\":29418}}],\"stop_reason\":\"tool_use\",\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":1913,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":75264,\"output_tokens\":153,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"thinking_tokens\":0},\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"stop_details\":null},\"attributionAgent\":\"general-purpose\",\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"72b6ebc2-4b6b-4ae0-b3d3-07b1bc31eb43\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-25T22:07:44.438Z\",\"effort\":\"high\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"sdk-cli\",\"cwd\":\"C:\\\\Svemir\\\\data\\\\sessions\\\\c1792946760393lb6a\\\\medijana_baza\\\\roj_glm\\\\objekti_CD\",\"sessionId\":\"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d\",\"version\":\"2.1.232\",\"gitBranch\":\"master\",\"slug\":\"cached-soaring-sedgewick\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"72b6ebc2-4b6b-4ae0-b3d3-07b1bc31eb43\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"promptId\":\"8f7a7d2d-dfff-49d8-9afd-b83bde684221\",\"agentId\":\"af3648b6823f6e54f\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"call_394132fe0ce147c0ac194367\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"29418\\t<dc:identifier>https://hdl.handle.net/21.15107/rcub_rai_977</dc:identifier>\\n29419\\t<dc:language>sr</dc:language>\\n29420\\t<dc:relation>info:eu-repo/grantAgreement/MESTD/Basic Research (BR or ON)/177007/RS//</dc:relation>\\n29421\\t<dc:rights>openAccess</dc:rights>\\n29422\\t<dc:rights>ARR</dc:rights>\\n29423\\t<dc:publisher>Београд : Дрштво за античке студије Србије</dc:publisher>\\n29424\\t<dc:source>Антика некад и сад: значај, улога и наслеђе кроз векове. 11. Међународни научни скуп, 16-17. децембар 2017, Књига резимеа</dc:source>\\n29425\\t</oai_dc:dc></metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:rai.ai.ac.rs:123456789/978</identifier><datestamp>2025-06-12T11:26:00Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_123456789_1</setSpec><setSpec>col_123456789_3</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc=\\\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/\\\" xmlns:doc=\\\"http://www.lyncode.com/xoai\\\" xmlns:xsi=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\\\" xmlns:dc=\\\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\\\" xsi:schemaLocation=\\\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd\\\">\\n29426\\t<dc:title>Representation of Medusa on a mosaic floor in Mediana</dc:title>\\n29427\\t<dc:creator>Jeremić, Gordana</dc:creator>\\n29428\\t<dc:contributor>Vujović, Miroslav B.</dc:contributor>\\n29429\\t<dc:subject>Mediana / villa with peristyle / aula / floor mosaic / Medusa / late antiquity / 4th century</dc:subject>\\n29430\\t<dc:description>A number of representative rooms decorated by mosaic floors from the period around the 4th century were examined during the archaeological research of the villa with peristyle in the middle of the late antiquity settlement in Mediana near Naissus. In 1969, a part of the damaged mosaic floor with geometrical motifs and a central round emblem including a representation of Medusa-Gorgon with wings was discovered in the central room of the villa, that is, in a large triclinium-aula. Medusa is represented in the manner of late antiquity, as a woman with a pensive expression who has lost many of the attributes characteristic of such representations in Greek and Hellenistic art. The aim of this paper is not only to provide analyses of the visual artistic aspect of the presentation but also to attempt a reconstruction of the mosaic carpet in the room on the basis of various site data, which are now available to researchers.</dc:description>\\n29431\\t<dc:date>2023-11-23T12:24:59Z</dc:date>\\n29432\\t<dc:date>2023-11-23T12:24:59Z</dc:date>\\n29433\\t<dc:date>2017</dc:date>\\n29434\\t<dc:type>bookPart</dc:type>\\n29435\\t<dc:type>publishedVersion</dc:type>\\n29436\\t<dc:identifier>978-86-6427-068-7</dc:identifier>\\n29437\\t<dc:identifier>https://rai.ai.ac.rs/handle/123456789/978</dc:identifier>\\n29438\\t<dc:identifier>http://rai.ai.ac.rs/bitstream/id/2209/05_ANTE_PORTAM_AUREAM_2017_Representation_of_Medusa_on_a_mosaic_floor.pdf</dc:identifier>\\n29439\\t<dc:identifier>https://hdl.handle.net/21.15107/rcub_rai_978</dc:identifier>\\n29440\\t<dc:language>en</dc:language>\\n29441\\t<dc:relation>info:eu-repo/grantAgreement/MESTD/Basic Research (BR or ON)/177007/RS//</dc:relation>\\n29442\\t<dc:rights>openAccess</dc:rights>\"}]},\"uuid\":\"9972fb32-682e-4cf5-b9b9-6b6997ea8239\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-25T22:07:44.456Z\",\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"72b6ebc2-4b6b-4ae0-b3d3-07b1bc31eb43\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"sdk-cli\",\"cwd\":\"C:\\\\Svemir\\\\data\\\\sessions\\\\c1792946760393lb6a\\\\medijana_baza\\\\roj_glm\\\\o