cal and imported products</dc:subject>\\n9483-<dc:subject>Middle Danube Limes</dc:subject>\\n9484-<dc:subject>4th to the beginning of 7th century</dc:subject>\\n9485-<dc:description>The paper deals with the Early Christian objects in the Middle Danube Limes from&#xd;\\n9486-Singidunum to Aquae. According to their function, shape or decorative content, it&#xd;\\n--\\n16165:<dc:creator>Jeremić, Gordana</dc:creator>\\n16166-<dc:creator>Lazić, Sara</dc:creator>\\n16167-<dc:creator>Vitezović, Selena</dc:creator>\\n16168-<dc:contributor>Miladinović-Radmilović, Nataša</dc:contributor>\\n16169-<dc:contributor>Vulović, Dragana</dc:contributor>\\n16170-<dc:contributor>Vitezović, Selena</dc:contributor>\\n16171-<dc:subject>Naissus</dc:subject>\\n16172-<dc:subject>spatula</dc:subject>\\n16173-<dc:subject>ruler</dc:subject>\\n--\\n27901:<dc:creator>Jeremić, Gordana</dc:creator>\\n27902-<dc:subject>Northern Illyricum</dc:subject>\\n27903-<dc:subject>Christianisation</dc:subject>\\n27904-<dc:subject>martyrs</dc:subject>\\n27905-<dc:subject>edicts</dc:subject>\\n27906-<dc:subject>episcopacies</dc:subject>\\n27907-<dc:subject>church buildings</dc:subject>\\n27908-<dc:subject>barbarians</dc:subject>\\n27909-<dc:subject>4th–6th/7th century</dc:subject>\\n--\\n27929:<dc:creator>Jeremić, Gordana</dc:creator>\\n27930-<dc:subject>Luxurious glass / glass workshops / Late Antiquity / Early Christianity / Roman provinces / Serbia</dc:subject>\\n27931-[Omitted long context line]\\n27932-<dc:date>2023-11-23T11:34:22Z</dc:date>\\n27933-<dc:date>2023-11-23T11:34:22Z</dc:date>\\n27934-<dc:date>2018</dc:date>\\n27935-<dc:type>conferenceObject</dc:type>\\n27936-<dc:type>publishedVersion</dc:type>\\n27937-<dc:identifier>https://rai.ai.ac.rs/handle/123456789/938</dc:identifier>\\n--\\n27949:<dc:creator>Jeremić, Gordana</dc:creator>\\n27950-<dc:creator>Čerškov, Toni</dc:creator>\\n27951-<dc:subject>Naissus / Niš / glass findings / vessels / windowpanes / necropolises / domus / Roman period / Late Antiquty</dc:subject>\\n27952-[Omitted long context line]\\n27953-<dc:date>2023-11-23T11:37:19Z</dc:date>\\n27954-<dc:date>2023-11-23T11:37:19Z</dc:date>\\n27955-<dc:date>2018</dc:date>\\n27956-<dc:type>conferenceObject</dc:type>\\n27957-<dc:type>publishedVersion</dc:type>\\n--\\n27970:<dc:creator>Jeremić, Gordana</dc:creator>\\n27971-<dc:creator>Vitezović, Selena</dc:creator>\\n27972-<dc:subject>Wild fauna / raw material / production / antler workshops / Roman limes / Upper Moesia</dc:subject>\\n27973-<dc:description>In this paper will be offered an overview of antler production and use on the borders in &#xd;\\n27974-Upper Moesia province. In Singidunum, on the location of the Castrum, an antler workshop &#xd;\\n27975-was discovered, with large quantities of antler segments with traces of manufacture. In the Iron &#xd;\\n27976-Gates region, antler artefacts were discovered at several fortifications, and the typological repertoire included awls, needles, spindle whorls, etc. Particularly numerous are combs (pecten), &#xd;\\n27977-discovered at several sites, including Saldum, Diana, Novae, and Pontes, and mainly originating &#xd;\\n27978-from the Late Antiquity period.<\\\\dc:description>\\n--\\n\\n[Showing results with pagination = limit: 120]\"}]},\"uuid\":\"fe424a56-e6da-4e48-8b7c-fad82adaf9e1\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-25T22:09:00.454Z\",\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"04d016db-eb92-4745-8010-0d4bf844c7e8\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"sdk-cli\",\"cwd\":\"C:\\\\Svemir\\\\data\\\\sessions\\\\c1792946760393lb6a\\\\medijana_baza\\\\roj_glm\\\\objekti_CD\",\"sessionId\":\"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d\",\"version\":\"2.1.232\",\"gitBranch\":\"master\",\"slug\":\"cached-soaring-sedgewick\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"fe424a56-e6da-4e48-8b7c-fad82adaf9e1\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"af3648b6823f6e54f\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"msg_20261026060901b5f8d08e4a514fb0\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thi