Narodnog muzeja Niš 9 (2000?), str. 21–36. Autor/ka je S. Drča (verovatno Sofija Drča, Narodni muzej Niš). Pronađi: da li je Zbornik Narodnog muzeja Niš 9 negde dostupan online (doiserbia.nb.rs, scindeks, Narodni muzej Niš nis.muzej / muzejnis.rs, archive.org), apstrakt, PDF, ili citate koji prenose sadržaj (mere objekta B, položaj, namena, nalazi, hronologija).\\n2. Janković-Mihaldžić 2001 — novac sa objekta B, Zbornik Narodnog muzeja Niš 10, str. 27–38 (nastavak istraživanja objekta B).\\n3. Bilo šta drugo o \\\"objektu B\\\" na Medijani (iskopni izveštaji, Arheološki pregled, Starinar, niški zbornici) — mere, položaj prema vili sa peristilom, tumačenje (šta je objekat B? rezidencija? privremeni boravak? vojni?).\\n\\nKLJUČNO PITANJE za širi projekat: u literaturi o Medijani objekti van vile sa peristilom nose oznake A, B, C, D. Ako naiđeš na objašnjenje šta su objekti A, C i D (mere, položaji, iskopavanja) — to je zlato, zapiši sve.\\n\\nPretraga na srpskom i engleskom: site:doiserbia.nb.rs mediana; site:doiserbia.nb.rs Drča; \\\"Zbornik Narodnog muzeja u Nišu\\\" 9 PDF; \\\"objekat B\\\" Medijana Drča; \\\"Sofija Drča\\\" arheologija; muzejnis.rs zbornik. Koristi WebSearch i WebFetch/mcp__web_reader__webReader.\\n\\nPAŽNJA — ZAMKA: mere \\\"objekat A 17,20×14,60 m / objekat B 20,30×14,18 / objekat C delimično\\\" su iz Mlinčića-Tisine kod Zenice (Arheološki pregled 11, Trajkovići), NE sa Medijane — ne primaj kao podatak o Medijani.\\n\\nNE piši nikakve fajlove. Vrati izveštaj kao čist tekst (srpski, latinica): za svaki pogodak — naslov, autor, godina, tačan URL, šta donosi (mere, položaji, nalazi, hronologija, šta su objekti A–D), nivo poverenja (visoko = pun tekst; srednje = apstrakt/citat; nisko = samo bibliografija). Na kraju iskreno šta je zatvoreno.\"},\"uuid\":\"94e66731-ba0c-4ac2-bef1-fdbc455d7a11\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-25T21:43:48.522Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"sdk-cli\",\"cwd\":\"C:\\\\Svemir\\\\data\\\\sessions\\\\c1792946760393lb6a\\\\medijana_baza\\\\roj_glm\\\\objekti_CD\",\"sessionId\":\"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d\",\"version\":\"2.1.232\",\"gitBranch\":\"master\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"94e66731-ba0c-4ac2-bef1-fdbc455d7a11\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a248fa135784f2c67\",\"attachment\":{\"type\":\"skill_listing\",\"content\":\"- dataviz: Use this skill whenever you are about to create ANY chart, graph, plot, dashboard, or data visualization, in ANY output medium — an HTML or React artifact, inline SVG, plotting code in any library (matplotlib, plotly, d3, Recharts, …), an image/PNG you will render and upload, or a chart shared into Slack. Read it BEFORE writing the first line of chart code, choosing chart colors, building a stat tile / meter / KPI row, or laying out a dashboard. Produces visualizations that read as one system — elegant, accessible, consistent in light and dark — using a brand-neutral placeholder palette you swap for your own. Teaches a design-system-agnostic method: a form heuristic, a color formula with a runnable validator, mark specs, and interaction rules. A validated default palette is documented in `references/palette.md` — swap that file's values for your brand's. Triggers on: \\\"chart\\\", \\\"graph\\\", \\\"plot\\\", \\\"data viz\\\", \\\"visualization\\\", \\\"dashboard\\\", \\\"analytics\\\", \\\"visualize data\\\", \\\"categorical colors\\\", \\\"sequential / diverging palette\\\", \\\"stat tile\\\", \\\"sparkline\\\", \\\"heatmap\\\", \\\"legend\\\", \\\"axis\\\", \\\"tooltip\\\", \\\"chart colors\\\", \\\"color by series\\\".\\n- update-config: Use this skill to configure the Claude Code harness via settings.json. Automated behaviors (\\\"from now on when X\\\", \\\"each time X\\\", \\\"whenever X\\\", \\\"before/after X\\\") require hooks configured in settings.json - the harness executes these, not Claude, so memory/preferences cannot fulfill them. Also use for: permissions (\\\"allow X\\\", \\\"add permission\\\", \\\"move permission to\\\"), env vars (\\\"set X=Y\\\"), hook troubleshooting, or any changes to settings.json/settings.local.json files. Examples: \\\"allow npm commands\\\", \\\"add bq permission to global settings\\\", \\\"move permission to user settings\\\", \\\"set DEBUG=true\\\", \\\"when claude stops show X\\\". For simple settings like theme/model, suggest the /config command.\\n- keybindings-help: Use when the user wants to customize keyboard shortcuts, rebind keys, add chord bindings, or modify ~/.claude/keybindings.json. Examples: \\\"rebind ctrl+s\\\", \\\"add a chord shortcut\\\", \\\"change the submit key\\\", \\\"customize keybindings\\\".\\n- simplify: Review the changed code for reuse, simplification, efficiency, and altitude cleanups, then apply the fixes. Quality only — it does not hunt for bugs; use /code-review for that.\\n- fewer-permission-prompts: Scan your transcripts for common read-only Bash and MCP tool calls, then add a prioritized allowlist to project .claude/settings.json to reduce permission prompts.\\n- loop: Run a prompt or slash command on a recurring interval (e.g. /loop 5m /foo, defaults to 10m) - When the user wants to set up a recurring task, poll for status, or run something repeatedly on an interval (e.g. \\\"check the deploy every 5 minutes\\\", \\\"keep running /babysit-prs\\\"). Do NOT invoke for one-off tasks.\\n- claude-api: Reference for the Claude API / Anthropic SDK — model ids, pricing, params, streaming, tool use, MCP, agents, caching, token counting, model migration.\\nTRIGGER — read BEFORE opening the target file; don't skip because it \\\"looks like a one-liner\\\" — whenever: the prompt names Claude/Anthropic in any form (Claude, Anthropic, Fable, Opus, Sonnet, Haiku, `anthropic`, `@anthropic-ai`, `claude-*`, `us.anthropic.*`, `[1m]`); the user asks about an LLM (pricing/model choice/limits/caching) — never answer from memory; OR the task is LLM-shaped with provider unstated (agent/MCP/tool-definition/multi-agent/RAG/LLM-judge/compute