{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261026061032d5924936d53e456a","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The Jeremić 2017 paper transmits:\n- Chronology: Vasić 2005: first construction phase after 317 (probably 319) until 330; around 330 most buildings destroyed/levelled; horreum, military barracks and villa with peristyle possibly built then; phase ends with Gothic destruction 378; smaller settlement with necropolis and two churches 378/380–441 (Huns); Vasić 2013 revised beginning to end of 3rd/beginning of 4th c. (following Petrović 1994, 22).\n- Settlement ~80 ha, >20 partly explored buildings + same number via geomagnetics (Milošević et al. 2011, 277 fig. 2).\n- Six buildings with mosaics (five residential + one early Christian church).\n- Aula: 19.6 × 12 m rectangular, apse depth 5.2 m on north end, hypocaust, studied 1969-1971; triclinium-aula interpretation.\n- Leda/fluvius panel at entrance; Medusa emblem 1969 in central room.\n- Photo credit \"photo: G. Milosevi\" — she photographed.\n\nThis is a citing work transmitting content relevant to the database. Already partially in the base (base has commit about Meduza aula etc.). Fine.\n\nNow — remaining crucial unknown: venue of \"Urbanism and Architecture of the Imperial Domain at Mediana\". Local evidence assembled:\n1. Milošević's known English papers: geophysics Starinar 61 (2011); \"Roman Naissus between the Archaeological Park and Modern Town\" (2006 congress abstract).\n2. Milošević 2013: \"Arhitektura rezidencijalnog kompleksa na Medijani\" in Konstantin Veliki i Milanski edikt 313 (Beograd 2013) 118-125 — Serbian.\n3. Monograph 2016: Konstantinova vila u Medijani / Constantine's Villa at Mediana (Niš 2016), open access at RAI.\n\nHypothesis: \"Urbanism and Architecture of the Imperial Domain at Mediana\" is the English-language chapter by Gordana Milošević inside the 2016 bilingual monograph \"Constantine's Villa at Mediana\" (or its English summary edition). The Academia upload would be that chapter. I could not verify the TOC because webReader is down.\n\nCan I verify locally? The oai_full.xml record 1539 has no chapter list. sr-wiki cites the monograph. Nothing more locally.\n\nLet me try webReader once more; if it works, targets in order:\na) https://rai.ai.ac.rs/handle/123456789/1539 (monograph record — maybe shows abstract only)\nb) http://rai.ai.ac.rs/bitstream/id/4423/bitstream_4423.pdf (PDF — webReader may extract text)\nc) api.semanticscholar.org title search\n\nActually — also worth trying: the coordinator's note says check \"Illyricum Romanum\" contents. The RAI record has no TOC. Maybe the book is on the AI website ai.ac.rs with TOC (publication page). URL guess: http://ai.ac.rs/... unknown. webReader needed.\n\nOne more local avenue: oai_2020.xml and oai_all.xml — earlier harvests; oai_full.xml presumably superset. Skip.\n\nfasti_search.html / fasti_n.html — Fasti Online search pages for Mediana; tapavicki_2011.txt is the Mediana 2011 Fasti record. Let me check those for excavation details (measures of objects C/D?). Quick greps. Also check aus2019/2020/2021 for thermae reports with measures (transmitting Milošević-era data? The thermae digs 2017-2022 led by Gavrilović Vitas). The task focuses on the Milošević paper, but excavation reports add context. Keep focus.\n\nLet me do: (1) webReader retry; (2) grep tapavicki_2011.txt header.","signature":"bfe74b3036a944e1930644c0"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"call_58909c1e0d5f4aed9a483050","session_id":"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d","uuid":"f95d4833-b06d-4fcf-8860-dc800fbbc145","timestamp":"2026-10-25T22:10:45.432Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Lov na Milošević Urbanism Mediana"}
