{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_10c8a1bfb7e543679ecebd37","type":"tool_result","content":"4818\t<dc:source>Starinar</dc:source>\n4819\t</oai_dc:dc></metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:rai.ai.ac.rs:123456789/254</identifier><datestamp>2026-07-24T08:24:30Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_123456789_1</setSpec><setSpec>col_123456789_3</setSpec><setSpec>col_123456789_413</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/\" xmlns:doc=\"http://www.lyncode.com/xoai\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\" xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\" xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd\">\n4820\t<dc:title>Stibadium B of villa with peristyle at Mediana</dc:title>\n4821\t<dc:creator>Gavrilović-Vitas, Nadežda</dc:creator>\n4822\t<dc:creator>Milošević-Jevtić, Gordana</dc:creator>\n4823\t<dc:creator>Crnoglavac, Vesna</dc:creator>\n4824\t<dc:description>In the course of archaeological investigations of the villa with peristyle in\n4825\t   2010 and 2011, a room of circular plan in the north-western segment of the\n4826\t   villa and to the north of room w-24, was discovered. The room had annexes in\n4827\t   the east and west and is analogous to the stibadium A discovered in the\n4828\t   north-eastern section of the villa. Further investigations of the room called\n4829\t   stibadium B revealed that the stibadium walls were decorated with a facing of\n4830\t   marble slabs and the floor was covered with exceptionally well preserved high\n4831\t   quality mosaic. Archaeological excavations in 2015 defined completely the\n4832\t   system of floor and wall heating. The mosaic floors in stibadium B are\n4833\t   conserved. The area to the west of the stibadium has also been explored and a\n4834\t   channel with the remains of a lead water pipe was discovered there. The\n4835\t   terrain to the north of the northern wall of the villa with peristyle was\n4836\t   also levelled.</dc:description>\n4837\t<dc:date>2022-05-10T11:26:55Z</dc:date>\n4838\t<dc:date>2022-05-10T11:26:55Z</dc:date>\n4839\t<dc:date>2016</dc:date>\n4840\t<dc:type>article</dc:type>\n4841\t<dc:type>publishedVersion</dc:type>\n4842\t<dc:identifier>0350-0241</dc:identifier>\n4843\t<dc:identifier>https://rai.ai.ac.rs/handle/123456789/254</dc:identifier>\n4844\t<dc:identifier>10.2298/STA1666081G</dc:identifier>\n4845\t<dc:identifier>http://rai.ai.ac.rs/bitstream/id/123/251.pdf</dc:identifier>\n4846\t<dc:relation>info:eu-repo/grantAgreement/MESTD/Basic Research (BR or ON)/177007/RS//</dc:relation>\n4847\t<dc:rights>openAccess</dc:rights>\n4848\t<dc:rights>https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/</dc:rights>\n4849\t<dc:rights>BY-NC-ND</dc:rights>\n4850\t<dc:publisher>Arheološki institut, Beograd</dc:publisher>\n4851\t<dc:source>Starinar</dc:source>\n4852\t</oai_dc:dc></metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:rai.ai.ac.rs:123456789/255</identifier><datestamp>2025-12-31T09:37:06Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_123456789_1</setSpec><setSpec>col_123456789_3</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/\" xmlns:doc=\"http://www.lyncode.com/xoai\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\" xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\" xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd\">\n4853\t<dc:title>Fishing with lure hooks at the Late Neolithic site of Vinca - Belo Brdo, Serbia</dc:title>\n4854\t<dc:creator>Cristiani, Emanuela</dc:creator>\n4855\t<dc:creator>Dimitrijević, Vesna</dc:creator>\n4856\t<dc:creator>Vitezović, Selena</dc:creator>\n4857\t<dc:subject>Vinca Culture</dc:subject>"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"call_58909c1e0d5f4aed9a483050","session_id":"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d","uuid":"7a08b9df-92b5-432b-a196-06239dd8a37c","timestamp":"2026-10-25T22:11:18.432Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Lov na Milošević Urbanism Mediana"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_48c94a77b88744c48f5dffea","type":"tool_result","content":"33545\t<dc:identifier>https://rai.ai.ac.rs/handle/123456789/1071</dc:identifier>\n33546\t<dc:identifier>https://hdl.handle.net/21.15107/rcub_rai_1071</dc:identifier>\n33547\t<dc:language>sr</dc:language>\n33548\t<dc:relation>info:eu-repo/grantAgreement/MESTD/Basic Research (BR or ON)/177007/RS//</dc:relation>\n33549\t<dc:relation>info:eu-repo/grantAgreement/MESTD/Basic Research (BR or ON)/177021/RS//</dc:relation>\n33550\t<dc:rights>restrictedAccess</dc:rights>\n33551\t<dc:rights>ARR</dc:rights>\n33552\t<dc:publisher>Неготин : Музеј Крајине</dc:publisher>\n33553\t<dc:source>Мокрањске стене, културна баштина Неготинске Крајине</dc:source>\n33554\t</oai_dc:dc></metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:rai.ai.ac.rs:123456789/1072</identifier><datestamp>2026-07-24T08:24:31Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_123456789_1</setSpec><setSpec>col_123456789_3</setSpec><setSpec>col_123456789_413</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/\" xmlns:doc=\"http://www.lyncode.com/xoai\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\" xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\" xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd\">\n33555\t<dc:title>Mokranjske stene. Rezultati istraživanja 2013. godine</dc:title>\n33556\t<dc:creator>Kapuran, Aleksandar</dc:creator>\n33557\t<dc:creator>Bulatović, Aleksandar</dc:creator>\n33558\t<dc:creator>Miladinović-Radmilović, Nataša</dc:creator>\n33559\t<dc:subject>Mokranjske Stene – Potkapina</dc:subject>\n33560\t<dc:subject>srednjovekovna nekropola</dc:subject>\n33561\t<dc:subject>XI–XIII vek</dc:subject>\n33562\t<dc:description>Tokom treće istraživačke kampanje na lokalitetu Mokranjske Stene – Potkapina, koji se nalazi oko 8 km jugoistočno od Negotina, istraživana je padina uzvišenja Sokolica, odnosno prostor extra muros, severno od vizantijskog utvrđenja. Na padini iznad lokalnog makadamskog puta, otvorene su dve sonde (sonda 3 i 4), od kojih je severnu (sonda 4) predstavljala dugačka lamela. Istraživanja prethodnih godina bila su koncentrisana isključivo na jugoistočnom delu lokaliteta (Popović, Kapuran 2011; Kapuran 2012; Kapuran, Milošević 2013).</dc:description>\n33563\t<dc:date>2023-11-27T12:26:58Z</dc:date>\n33564\t<dc:date>2023-11-27T12:26:58Z</dc:date>\n33565\t<dc:date>2014</dc:date>\n33566\t<dc:type>bookPart</dc:type>\n33567\t<dc:type>publishedVersion</dc:type>\n33568\t<dc:identifier>978-86-80093-93-2</dc:identifier>\n33569\t<dc:identifier>https://rai.ai.ac.rs/handle/123456789/1072</dc:identifier>\n33570\t<dc:identifier>https://hdl.handle.net/21.15107/rcub_rai_1072</dc:identifier>\n33571\t<dc:language>sr</dc:language>\n33572\t<dc:relation>info:eu-repo/grantAgreement/MESTD/Basic Research (BR or ON)/177020/RS//</dc:relation>\n33573\t<dc:rights>restrictedAccess</dc:rights>\n33574\t<dc:rights>ARR</dc:rights>"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"call_58909c1e0d5f4aed9a483050","session_id":"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d","uuid":"ba492915-1a1e-4038-ba3e-acb68cebf208","timestamp":"2026-10-25T22:11:18.440Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Lov na Milošević Urbanism Mediana"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202610260611101f01fef3a9e64654","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Weird — with -i and -o, \"objekat\" returns nothing, but without -o it matched lines 20, 127. That means the match at lines 20/127 was for the \"Drc?a\" pattern (\"Dra\"? e.g. \"Dra~\" something like \" obala\"? no... \"Dra\" appears in e.g. \"Dra\" words? With -i, \"Dra\" matches inside many words like \"Draudžina\"? Hmm \"dra\" as substring — \"Хиландара\"? No that's Cyrillic. \"Mljekara\"? no. Words containing \"dra\": \"Zemun—Begrada\"? \"Beograda\" contains \"dra\"? B-e-o-g-r-a-d-a: \"dra\"? no, that's \"ada\". \"Beogradu\"? no. \"obrađ...\"; \"Petrograd\"? Hmm. \"dubrov...\"; Actually \"Medijana... Brzi Brod\"? \"Brod\"? no. \"Dard...\"? Let me not guess: \"Dra\" with -i matches \"дра\"? no, different script. \"beogradskog\"? no.\n\nEh, whatever — likely \"Dra\" matched something like \"Zapadna\" (\"za-DRA-...no\"). \"Zapadna\": z-a-p-a-d-n-a — no \"dra\". \"Srednja\"? no. \"obradi\"? \"u obradi\" — o-b-r-a-d-i: \"rad\" reversed... \"obradi\" contains \"rad\" not \"dra\". \"Nedeljković\"? no. \"Драyт\"? The wikitext is Serbian Wikipedia — mostly Cyrillic. \"objekat\" in Cyrillic is \"објекат\"! My grep \"objekat\" wouldn't match Cyrillic \"објекат\". And \"Drča\" in Cyrillic \"Дрча\". That's why: the file is in Cyrillic!\n\nLet me grep for Cyrillic patterns: \"објекат\" and \"Дрча\".","signature":"a96c3bec5ca648929e22c7db"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"call_586b64b53f2445699ef01253","session_id":"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d","uuid":"a542d9d8-b51d-46ff-b866-ed184958e27f","timestamp":"2026-10-25T22:11:19.136Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Lov na Drča 2000 objekat B"}
