imited in MY thread — but agents have their own web_reader access? The a7308 agent tried web_reader too and got 429. Hmm.\n\n2. Agent af3648 (Jeremić): aus2019 bibliography line 7234: a 2019 publication vol 35, 65-83 by likely Gavrilović-Vitas about Mediana thermae. Also tapavicki_2011.txt fully read (already known).\n\n3. Agent a248f (Drča): found talas_v015.js line 406: 'Drča S. 2000, Medijana — objekat B, Zbornik Narodnog muzeja Niš 9, 21-36 + Janković-Mihaldžić 2001 (novac sa objekta B), Zbornik NN 10, 27-38' — the base already knows Drča 2000 + Janković-Mihaldžić 2001 coin report from object B. Good — that's a second reference: Janković-Mihaldžić 2001, Zbornik Narodnog muzeja Niš 10, 27–38, \"novac sa objekta B\".\n\nNow my move: web_reader is 429 in my thread. The agents are running with their own attempts. Rather than duplicating, I should:\n1. Wait for agent notifications (they'll arrive).\n2. Meanwhile, try the ONE key URL myself when rate limit frees: the Jeremić 2006 PDF at ubnt.ni.ac.rs. Actually — maybe try now? I just got 429 a minute ago. The rate limit seems to be per-MCP-server daily quota perhaps. My earlier attempts failed repeatedly.\n\nAlternative channels I haven't tried in this session: WebFetch tool (built-in) — earlier \"requested permissions haven't granted\". WebSearch — denied earlier. Bash curl — requires approval. So my only channel is mcp web_reader (429).\n\nHmm — but wait: the agents presumably have the same web_reader. One of them got 429 too. But maybe the rate limit is per-thread/per-minute. Let me try once more in a bit.\n\nActually, let me think about what remains for MY work:\n- Write nalaz.md + mera.json. I have a LOT of material already.\n- Key missing: objects C and D specifics. What do we know about \"objekat C\" and \"objekat D\" at Medijana? From the base (SINTEZA v0.15 + talas_v015.js line 395-406): Drča 2000 objekat B Zbornik NMN 9, 21-36; Janković-Mihaldžić 2001 novac sa objekta B. The Zenica trap was recorded. Do we know what objekat B at Medijana IS? The SINTEZA says base v0.15 knows the reference but presumably not full content.\n\nFrom sr-wiki and literature: buildings at Medijana outside the villa: horreum (1936), vojne barake, terme, vila sa oktogonom, vila sa konhama (1975), vodotoranj, crkve... The A-D lettering system in Narodni muzej Niš literature — objekat B (Drča 2000). What are A, C, D? Without the actual Drča 2000 text, we can't say definitively. Candidates: the letters might designate buildings south of the villa / along the road.\n\nActually — I recall from the summary: \"sistem oznaka: stibadium A i B su UNUTAR vile → Drčin 'objekat B' (2000) je drugi sistem oznaka\". The monograph 2016 (vila+terme+kapija) is the main candidate to resolve. The \"antique gate\" (kapija) in the 2016 monograph description! \"large villa with peristyle, thermae and antique gate\" — the gate could be objekat D or similar.\n\nMy best play now:\n1. Try web_reader once more (maybe on the Jeremić 2006 ubnt PDF — highest value per byte).\n2. If still 429, start drafting nalaz.md + mera.json from the extensive material I have (I can draft now and update if agents deliver).\n3. Agents will notify on completion; incorporate.\n\nActually, drafting now is wise — I have rich material. But first one more web_reader attempt, since several minutes passed. Actually I literally just tried (first tool call this turn) and got 429. It's a persistent quota. Let me not burn calls; instead draft.\n\nWait — one more consideration: the srwiki wikitext is on disk. Let me extract the Jeremić 2006 PDF URL from it precisely (line 198 cite). The URL: http://www.ubnt.ni.ac.rs/images/pdf/nisivizantija/Nis%20i%20Vizantija%20-%2004_2005/10_Jeremic_Gordana.pdf. I should try this via web_reader — one attempt. If 429, note it and delegate/wait.\n\nAlso from the wikitext (already read by agent, and I saw the content): villa with conchae details cited to 2016 monograph; Petrović 1994 situational plan with numbered objects 1-15 (line 190 caption: 1 villa with peristyl, 2 thermae, 3 nymphaeum, 4 horreum west, water tower 5 south, fortress 6, villa with conchae 7, villa with fence wall 8, villa 9, villa with central corridor 10, horreum II 11, sacral objects 12,13, vicus 14, necropolis 15). This is the Petrović 1994 plan (p. 22)! Numbers, not letters. So A-D letters are NOT from Petrović 1994 plan — they're from NMN internal literature (Drča 2000). Good to record: two systems (numbers 1994; letters NMN 2000s).\n\nLet me now:\n1. Read srwiki wikitext around lines 190-226 myself to capture the exact captions + refs (I have the content from the agent output above — actually I have it verbatim in the TaskOutput. No need to re-read).\n2. Try web_reader once on the Jeremić 2006 PDF URL.\n3. Draft nalaz.md and mera.json.\n\nThe summary says I can start writing. The agents may still deliver Drča/Jeremić/Milošević findings; I'll incorporate when notifications arrive, before finalizing. But the user asked: \"na kraju predaj nalaz.md\" — deliver at end. The session already restarted once; best to have files on disk ASAP, then update.\n\nLet me try web_reader on Jeremić 2006 PDF first.","signature":"875570662aa54f908831225a"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d","uuid":"d7e2834e-8824-4810-9534-bb373e583207","timestamp":"2026-10-25T22:12:32.437Z"}
