{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_510074f67db744c9bad6e122","type":"tool_result","content":"3092\t<dc:title>Excavations of Mediana in 2010 and 2011</dc:title>\n3093\t<dc:creator>Vasić, Miloje</dc:creator>\n3094\t<dc:creator>Milošević, Gordana</dc:creator>\n3095\t<dc:creator>Gavrilović, Nadežda</dc:creator>\n3096\t<dc:subject>Medijana</dc:subject>\n3097\t<dc:subject>vila s peristilom</dc:subject>\n3098\t<dc:subject>stratigrafija</dc:subject>\n3099\t<dc:subject>arhitektura</dc:subject>\n3100\t<dc:subject>pokretni nalazi</dc:subject>\n3101\t<dc:subject>kasna antika</dc:subject>\n3102\t<dc:description>Throughout 2010 and 2011, a systematic nine month archaeological exploration\n3103\t   was conducted on the north-eastern, northwestern and south-eastern parts of\n3104\t   the villa with peristyle, as well as the area in front of the museum building\n3105\t   (see note 8). The envisaged area of exploration was around 1,400 m². In\n3106\t   total, 1,230 m² of this area was thoroughly examined (Fig. 1). The\n3107\t   excavations were performed with the aim of defining the dimensions of the\n3108\t   north-western and south-western parts of the villa, the appearance of the\n3109\t   villa’s entrance, as well as to explore the foundations of the museum\n3110\t   building. In the course of the excavations, certain differences were\n3111\t   perceived in the stratigraphy of the villa with peristyle and the part\n3112\t   excavated outside the villa.</dc:description>\n3113\t<dc:date>2022-05-10T11:23:58Z</dc:date>\n3114\t<dc:date>2022-05-10T11:23:58Z</dc:date>\n3115\t<dc:date>2014</dc:date>\n3116\t<dc:type>article</dc:type>\n3117\t<dc:type>publishedVersion</dc:type>\n3118\t<dc:identifier>0350-0241</dc:identifier>\n3119\t<dc:identifier>https://rai.ai.ac.rs/handle/123456789/210</dc:identifier>\n3120\t<dc:identifier>10.2298/STA1464231V</dc:identifier>\n3121\t<dc:identifier>http://rai.ai.ac.rs/bitstream/id/92/207.pdf</dc:identifier>\n3122\t<dc:rights>openAccess</dc:rights>\n3123\t<dc:rights>https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/</dc:rights>\n3124\t<dc:rights>BY-NC-ND</dc:rights>\n3125\t<dc:publisher>Arheološki institut, Beograd</dc:publisher>\n3126\t<dc:source>Starinar</dc:source>"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"call_586b64b53f2445699ef01253","session_id":"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d","uuid":"81baf7e5-2e55-42cc-a39b-21e9fabf6a7d","timestamp":"2026-10-25T22:25:14.807Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Lov na Drča 2000 objekat B"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_bb997ee293be44899aa63cbb","type":"tool_result","content":"4820\t<dc:title>Stibadium B of villa with peristyle at Mediana</dc:title>\n4821\t<dc:creator>Gavrilović-Vitas, Nadežda</dc:creator>\n4822\t<dc:creator>Milošević-Jevtić, Gordana</dc:creator>\n4823\t<dc:creator>Crnoglavac, Vesna</dc:creator>\n4824\t<dc:description>In the course of archaeological investigations of the villa with peristyle in\n4825\t   2010 and 2011, a room of circular plan in the north-western segment of the\n4826\t   villa and to the north of room w-24, was discovered. The room had annexes in\n4827\t   the east and west and is analogous to the stibadium A discovered in the\n4828\t   north-eastern section of the villa. Further investigations of the room called\n4829\t   stibadium B revealed that the stibadium walls were decorated with a facing of\n4830\t   marble slabs and the floor was covered with exceptionally well preserved high\n4831\t   quality mosaic. Archaeological excavations in 2015 defined completely the\n4832\t   system of floor and wall heating. The mosaic floors in stibadium B are\n4833\t   conserved. The area to the west of the stibadium has also been explored and a\n4834\t   channel with the remains of a lead water pipe was discovered there. The\n4835\t   terrain to the north of the northern wall of the villa with peristyle was\n4836\t   also levelled.</dc:description>\n4837\t<dc:date>2022-05-10T11:26:55Z</dc:date>\n4838\t<dc:date>2022-05-10T11:26:55Z</dc:date>\n4839\t<dc:date>2016</dc:date>\n4840\t<dc:type>article</dc:type>\n4841\t<dc:type>publishedVersion</dc:type>\n4842\t<dc:identifier>0350-0241</dc:identifier>\n4843\t<dc:identifier>https://rai.ai.ac.rs/handle/123456789/254</dc:identifier>\n4844\t<dc:identifier>10.2298/STA1666081G</dc:identifier>\n4845\t<dc:identifier>http://rai.ai.ac.rs/bitstream/id/123/251.pdf</dc:identifier>\n4846\t<dc:relation>info:eu-repo/grantAgreement/MESTD/Basic Research (BR or ON)/177007/RS//</dc:relation>\n4847\t<dc:rights>openAccess</dc:rights>\n4848\t<dc:rights>https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/</dc:rights>\n4849\t<dc:rights>BY-NC-ND</dc:rights>\n4850\t<dc:publisher>Arheološki institut, Beograd</dc:publisher>\n4851\t<dc:source>Starinar</dc:source>\n4852\t</oai_dc:dc></metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:rai.ai.ac.rs:123456789/255</identifier><datestamp>2025-12-31T09:37:06Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_123456789_1</setSpec><setSpec>col_123456789_3</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/\" xmlns:doc=\"http://www.lyncode.com/xoai\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\" xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\" xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd\">\n4853\t<dc:title>Fishing with lure hooks at the Late Neolithic site of Vinca - Belo Brdo, Serbia</dc:title>\n4854\t<dc:creator>Cristiani, Emanuela</dc:creator>"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"call_586b64b53f2445699ef01253","session_id":"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d","uuid":"afae07a0-ac76-465b-a530-938b69a5b7a0","timestamp":"2026-10-25T22:25:14.815Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Lov na Drča 2000 objekat B"}
