{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_2026102606251569354e29f53146d1","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"These are about the villa itself, stibadia A and B (interior features) — NOT the \"objekat A/B/C/D\" labeling of separate buildings. Important distinction to convey in the report: in RAI/Starinar literature, \"stibadium A/B\" are dining pavilions of the villa; the \"objekat B\" of Drča 2000 is a separate building (Zbornik NMN).\n\nNow let me also read the descriptions of: 1756 (Venus or Diana), 44019 (Dionysus), 45786 (Latest Mosaics), 49776 (Medijana 2011). And importantly check \"Stambeni objekat iz poznog bronzanog doba... Medijana-sektor jug\" in oai_all.xml:2519 — that's prehistoric, \"Medijana — sektor jug\" (sector south). Not Roman objekat B.\n\nLet me read 44019 and 45786 descriptions.","signature":"6f34abfac5e2429f866ed6ba"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"call_586b64b53f2445699ef01253","session_id":"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d","uuid":"cdb9a9f4-2957-42e0-819f-ed40d4b75024","timestamp":"2026-10-25T22:25:19.180Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Lov na Drča 2000 objekat B"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261026062301d8f63d8dab9d478c","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting! The embed returns garbled Cyrillic — it IS the content but with a character-substitution cipher (Scribd obfuscation). Actually this looks like a ROT-style substitution applied to Cyrillic text. Notice patterns: \"Епднѝж Епднѝжбж\" — hmm. Let me try to decode: the substitution maps Cyrillic letters shifted. Let me check \"Ешлпѝж Епднѝжбж\" = \"Гордана Јеремић\"? Compare: Е→Г, ш→о, л→р, п→д, ѝ→а, ж→н. So \"Ешлпѝж\" = Г-о-р-д-а-н-а = \"Гордана\"! Yes! The cipher is a consistent per-letter substitution.\n\nCheck \"Епднѝжбж\": Е→Г? wait Е mapped to Г. п→д, д→ј? Hmm \"Епднѝжбж\" should be \"Јеремић\": Е→Ј? But earlier Е→Г in Ешлпѝж→Гордана. Hmm, first letter Е appears as both Г and Ј? Unless my mapping is wrong. Let me redo: \"Ешлпѝж\" — 6 letters: Е,ш,л,п,ѝ,ж → Г,о,р,д,а,н. So Е→Г, ш→о, л→р, п→д, ѝ→а, ж→н. Then \"Епднѝжбж\" — Е,п,д,н,ѝ,ж,б,ж → Г,д,?,?,а,н,?,н — that doesn't give Јеремић (7 letters: Ј,е,р,е,м,и,ћ). Hmm 8 vs 7.\n\nWait — maybe the text is not a simple substitution of Serbian Cyrillic; maybe the font encoding is shifted per-glyph and some glyphs map oddly. The italic ligatures could complicate. Actually, maybe it's simpler: this looks like a Cyrillic +1/-N shift in Unicode code points? Г is U+0413, Е is U+0415 — difference +2. о is U+043E, ш is U+0448 — difference -10. Not uniform shift. So it's an arbitrary substitution table (Scribd's anti-scraping font cipher), consistent per character across the document. It's decodable with frequency analysis since we know the language! And actually we can bootstrap the mapping from known words.\n\nBut hold on — the deliverable needs data: mere osnova objekata A/B/C/D, položaji, bibliografija. This embed page 49 (page number \"49\" at top... actually \"<49\" might be \"149\" with 1 dropped?) — the snippet mentions: \"ш ьваѝаѝ дцшиаѝ ицжђпвнбьоаѝ фжлн дамнкж ѝп маижтш шбштцжэўш дпоацжщнѝш\" — let me decode with partial mapping: ш→о, ь→?, в→?, а→?, ѝ→а, д→ј... hmm this is getting complex but the mapping seems consistent. Let me collect mappings from anchors:\n\nFrom \"Ешлпѝж\" = \"Гордана\": Е→Г, ш→о, л→р, п→д, ѝ→а, ж→н\nFrom \"Епднѝж Епднѝжбж\" context \"лицждж Ешлпѝж Епднѝжбж\" — should be \"др Гордана Јеремић\" or \"Dr Gordana Jeremic\"? \"лицждж\" = д-р? л→р (already), и→?, ц→?, ж→н (already), д→?, ж→н. Hmm \"лицждж\" 5 letters vs \"др\" 2. No.\n\nAlternatively the title line \"Kgrdl`l Noroac}\" at the top of the page — that's Latin transliteration cased weirdly: \"Kgrdl`l Noroac}\" — shift each letter by -2? K→I, g→e, r→p, d→b, l→j, `→^? Hmm \"Kgrdl`l\" -2 → \"Iepbj`j\"? Not it. Try +/− shifts: K-g-r-d-l-`-l → maybe \"Jeremic\"? J→K (+1), e→g (+2)? No.\n\nActually \"Kgrdl`l Noroac}\" — if we shift letters back by 2: K→I, g→e, r→p, d→b... \"Iepbj`j\". Shift forward 2: M... no. What about the pattern \"Noroac}\" = \"Mozaici\"? N→M (-1), o→o (0), r→z?? no.\n\nHmm, maybe each letter shifted by +1 with case: \"Noroac\" → \"Mosaik\"? N-1=M, o-1=n... no.\n\nActually — it's per-document random substitution, both Latin and Cyrillic scripts use separate tables. This is Scribd's obfuscated text layer (they map glyphs). Decoding by hand is possible but heavy for 14 pages. However, the DDG snippets already gave us clean text of page 1. What we need: objects A/B/C/D mentions. The embed page shown (49 = probably p. 149+) already decoded partially: I see \"Еалжныон зад Ёп заоцнвжа завцэнбш ад аоа ??е² (ьк. 8)\" — decode: Еалжныон = \"Мозаиком\"? Е→? wait now Е→М? Inconsistent again...\n\nHmm, actually maybe NOT one-to-one: \"Ешлпѝж\"→\"Гордана\" and \"Еалжныон\"→\"Мозаиком\" would need Е→Г AND Е→М. Contradiction → so the cipher is positional/rotating. That kills manual decoding.\n\nLet me instead grab the OTHER pages of the embed: Scribd embeds paginate via ?start_page=N or /content?start_page=... Actually modern Scribd embed uses page param: https://www.scribd.com/embeds/462516922/content?start_page=2 etc. The content returned above is page 2 of the doc (marked 49? confusing).\n\nWait — actually look: the returned text starts \"<49\\nKgrdl`l Noroac}\\nаоа 9=66 е\" — \"аоа 9=66 е\" could be \"низа 4/2005\" obfuscated? And \"Kgrdl`l Noroac}\" = \"Gordana Jeremic\" in Latin with a rotating Caesar cipher (each char +k rotating). Let me test rotating +1: K→J? K-1=J yes! g-1=f no... rotating means shift increments each character. K(-1)=J, g(-2)=e, r(-3)=o, d(-4)=`... no \"Jeremic\": J,e,r,e,m,i,c. K→J shift -1; g→e shift -2; r→r shift 0... inconsistent.\n\nOK, abandon cryptanalysis — too costly for deadline. The important thing: I FOUND the paper full text is accessible on Scribd (14 pages) and live PDF URLs. But can I get readable full text? One more approach: Scribd has a mobile/print endpoint? Not without auth.\n\nAlternative: Google cache of the nisandbyzantium PDF? Dead. \n\nWhat about r.jina.ai on the ubnt legacy URL — earlier jina attempt failed network. The webReader fetches server-side from China; scribd worked, DDG worked, nisandbyzantium/ubnt/jina all network-fail. Possibly those hosts block the reader's egress region or are slow. Try once more the nisandbyzantium URL with underscores? No — filename fixed.\n\nTry Wayback via a different mirror: archive.ph? URL: https://archive.ph/newest/https://www.nisandbyzantium.org.rs/doc/zbornik4/PDF-IV/Gordana Jeremic.pdf — spaces again. archive.ph requires exact URL. Could submit via the ubnt one? Both have spaces.\n\nHmm — what about Google Docs viewer: https://docs.google.com/viewer?url=<encoded> — needs %20 → -400.\n\nWhat about the `sl_h` DDG redirect for the nisandbyzantium result — the redirect goes through duckduckgo.com/l/?uddg=... which is percent-encoded → -400.\n\nOK — one more realistic avenue: the embed with start_page parameter to walk remaining pages, and try to decode enough around \"A\", \"B\", \"C\", \"D\" mentions. But cipher is rotating; however! The rendered markers like \"C\" appear literally: \"ш дамж Оабьтжбтнбж C\" — \"у вили ...објекат C\"? wait: \"Оабьтжбтнбж C\" — C is literal! And earlier \"зцаьтацж\" = \"објекат\"? Let me test: з→о? In \"Ешлпѝж\"→\"Гордана\" we had п→д. Try \"зцаьтацж\"→\"објекат\": з→о, ц→б, а→ј, ь→е, т→к, а→а?? — а→ј AND а→а contradiction... unless the cipher is rotating (positional). Yes rotating. So partial manual decode is unreliable.\n\nBUT the literal \"C\" in \"Оабьтжбтнбж C\" strongly suggests \"објекат C\" — hmm wait actually maybe it's \"грађевин? C\". And \"??\" digits got eaten (\"ад аоа ??е²\" — digits were dropped by the reader, shown as ?).\n\nInteresting: \"Оабьтжбтнбж C\" — if rotating cipher, the uppercase C stayed because the obfuscation only remaps lowercase? Look: \"Ешлпѝж\" has caps Е unchanged? No wait, if Е were unchanged it'd be \"Е\"=\"Е\"... but we deduced Е→Г. Hmm unless the actual author line is \"Гордана Јеремић\" printed and \"Ешлпѝж Епднѝжбж\" is something else entirely. \n\nHonestly, decoding is a rabbit hole. Priority per coordinator: data on objects A–D + bibliography. The Scribd doc page numbering: 14 pages = 145–158 exactly matches! The embed returned what appears to be p. 149-ish (mid-paper, discussing termе? \"трефопејум\"? The garbled \"фжлн дамнкж ѝп маижтш шбштцжэўш дпоацжщнѝш\" likely = \"хоројум и питома дивљач (тетреб?)\"... The passage mentions \"објекат C\" explicitly with a heated floor (пOrDefault \"з цпдьтжвае закшкпйпњпи цпыбаи ма-йжбьтвж (uvcus)\" — \"у подножју оградног зида парка (therces?)\"... This is likely the passage about the \" ekonomска celina / villa rustica\" with uvcus = \"parcus\"? Actually \"uvcus\" — de-substitute: u→p? v→a? c→r? u→c? s→s? → \"parcs\"? Hmm \"uvcus\" with the noted shift u-1=t, v-1=u, c-1=b... \"tubts\"? no. Given \"(uvcus)\" is Latin italic in parens — could be \"vivarium\"! v-i-v-a-r-i-u-m — 8 chars vs 5. Could be \"parcus\"/\"porcus\"... Actually likely \"thercop... \" hmm. The context \"у подножју оградног зида парка (?)\" + \"хорти/живина и птица... свиње\" — this is about the vivarium/zoo at Medijana! Jeremić 2006 discussing the \"живинарник\"? OK.\n\nGiven deadline: \"Ako ništa, predaj izveštaj\" — I now HAVE substantially more than before: live URLs for full text (nisandbyzantium + ubnt legacy + Scribd), confirmation the paper treats Medijana settlement 40 ha, objects including \"објекат C\" mention. But I can't cleanly extract.\n\nLet me make ONE more attempt to get clean text: Scribd embeds sometimes expose per-page JSONP at https://www.scribd.com/embeds/462516922/content?start_page=1&maximum_pages=... or the \"doc_page\" list. Actually there's also html.scribdassets.com pagejson. Too deep.\n\nBetter: try webReader on ubnt legacy WITHOUT plus — maybe the reader handles the space if I pass the URL trimmed? It auto-encodes? Try: https://www.ubnt.ni.ac.rs/legacy/images/pdf/nisivizantija/Nis i Vizantija - 04_2005/10_Jeremic_Gordana.pdf with literal spaces — reader might accept (it accepts spaces in DDG query? no, I used +). Try once — if -400, stop.\n\nActually earlier DDG-derived snippet came FROM these PDFs, meaning DDG crawled them. Google also has them cached. Try Bing cache? cn.bing garbage.\n\nOne more: Yandex? https://yandex.com/search/?text=... likely captcha.\n\nDecision: try literal-space ubnt legacy once; if fail → also try start_page walk on Scribd embed for pages containing A/B/D mentions (each page = one call; 14 pages = too many; but maybe the embed returns several pages at once? It returned what looks like 1-2 pages). The returned block began mid-sentence at \"49\" — likely only one page per call. The page shown mentions објекат C! If A/B/D are on adjacent pages... The order in such papers: A, B, C, D likely sequential. Page 149 showed C near end (\"ш дамж Оабьтжбтнбж C\"?). Hmm actually \"Оабьтжбтнбж\" might be \"грађевинsk?\" I can't trust.\n\nTry start_page=3 (next page) — it should have D and/or terme. And start_page=1 for A/B. That's 2 calls. Decoding rotating cipher manually for mere — I could pattern-match digits: \"аоа ??е²\" digits dropped... The cipher even eats digits (shown as ? and =66 for 4? \"аоа 9=66 е\" maybe \"низа 4/2006\"?). Numbers unreliable.\n\nHonestly: even undeciphered, I can note the Scribd/official URLs as HIGH-confidence sources for the coordinator to fetch directly (they work from a normal browser). The coordinator asked me to try; I should report the working URLs — that's a real win — plus what DDG snippets give.\n\nLet me do the two embed page calls, then finalize. Actually wait — does the embed support start_page? Old API: https://www.scribd.com/embeds/462516922/content?start_page=3&viewport=... Modern one might ignore. Try start_page=1 to see if content differs (if identical, abandon).","signature":"81a94d68eb64443eaf3fec5e"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"call_228a9101adba430ca741f6e2","session_id":"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d","uuid":"c8244899-fc12-45d3-9eb3-4a18583d1d84","timestamp":"2026-10-25T22:25:19.286Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Lov na Jeremić 2006 mozaici"}
