{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261026062543af7844339fb94040","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The sr.wiki article doesn't use \"objekat A/B/C/D\" for separate buildings — it names them (villa with peristyle, thermae, villa with octagon, villa with conchae, horreum, water tower, barracks, churches 1-2, baptistery). Notably: \"During the latest research (2000), a hoard and part of the bronze fence were discovered in Mediana\" — excavations in 2000! Drča 2000 \"Medijana — objekat B\" was published in Zbornik NN 9 (2000) — about the 2000 campaign? Hmm, actually Zbornik NN 9 published 2000-2001 would cover 1998-1999 excavations. But interesting: the bronze railing hoard was found in 2000 (Vasić). Janković-Mihaldžić 2001 \"novac sa objekta B\" in Zbornik NN 10.\n\nThe churches 1 and 2 were excavated 2000-2001 and 2007 by Vasić's team. Not \"objekat B\".\n\nI know from the project context (talas_v015.js): base already records 'Drča S. 2000, Medijana — objekat B, Zbornik Narodnog muzeja Niš 9, 21-36 + Janković-Mihaldžić 2001 (novac sa objekta B), Zbornik NN 10, 27-38'.\n\nTime check: I've spent a lot of turns. Let me try webReader once more; then a couple of key URLs if it works. If still 429, I'll compose the final report with what I have, honestly stating what's closed.\n\nActually — wait. Let me reconsider the webReader rate limit. All my calls have been 429 from the very start. The parent and other agents also seem to be getting 429s (gb quota dead, fasti api error). Maybe the webReader service is broken/exhausted for the whole session day. One more attempt now, then final attempt after a few minutes, then report.","signature":"addc0e65b29b43998899ee07"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"call_586b64b53f2445699ef01253","session_id":"715a8e85-940b-40be-aca9-e0e9c9f6c39d","uuid":"939b3527-cab6-4cd9-a