y wait — let me reconsider. The system message after my main-thread Write attempt just said \"you haven't granted it yet\" — no explicit user denial visible. The subagent got hard-denied. Maybe subagent tool permissions are always denied and main thread prompts are pending. It costs little to try once more with the final merged content — the content differs substantially (merged agent reports). Let me do it.\n\nMerged nalaz.md updates:\n- Section 0: update counts (14 skupina mera now with the 40-ha-verbatim?), Jeremić 2006 „tri živa URL-a\".\n- Section 1 table: museum page row (no letters, official description); parent speculation note.\n- Section 2.1: add Jeremić-agent findings? No — 2.1 is Milošević. Add to 2.2: Jeremić 2006 confirmed publisher/pages/URLs; 2007 oktogon Naissus URLs; 2010 disertacija str. 98–99; identity profile links; „objekat C\" Scribd lead (unreliable).\n- Section 2.3: Drča = Slobodan Drča; Latković–Drča 1979 vodič; muzej sajt Zbornik page dead end; doiserbia exclusion; Naissus 1/2008 expanded coin catalogues (NEW sub-item).\n- Section 2.5: add museum page description (high confidence), AUS 2015 read-blocked already there.\n- Section 3 citatna mreža: add museum page, bibliografije.nb.rs, DDG snippet method.\n- Section 6 limitations: add webReader -500 on ubnt/nisandbyzantium hosts (beyond 429); scribd obfuscation.\n- Section 7: reorder — Jeremić 2006 has 3 live URLs; monografija first still.\n\nmera.json — mostly unchanged; the 40-ha side of the conflict is now VERBATIM confirmed from Jeremić 2006's first page via DDG snippet (upgrade its confidence from \"srednje\" note to noting verbatim confirmation; keep conflict entry). Also could add nothing else with numbers. Jeremić 2017 pages 251–262 refinement in source strings.\n\nLet me write the updated nalaz.md (one more attempt), then mera.json (one attempt), then final message with 5-10 line summary + DONE. If Writes fail, final message includes the content pointer: tell user content is ready an